Article 7-3 (Special Cases of Tax Refund following Retroactive Deduction of Losses of Small or Medium Enterprise) (1)"Amount calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 8-4 means an amount determined according to either of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Where the person engaging in a small or medium enterprise is a resident: An amount calculated by subtracting the amount of item (b) from the amount of item (a):
    (a) An amount of global income tax on the small or medium enterprise, as calculated for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year;
    (b) An amount of global income tax on the small or medium enterprise, as calculated by applying the tax rate for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year to the amount calculated by subtracting losses incurred in the taxable year in which December 31, 2021 falls and carried forward under Article 45 (3) of the Income Tax Act (excluding losses incurred from a real estate leasing business and carried forward under paragraph (2) of that Article), for which the person wishes to be granted a retroactive tax credit (limited to the global income tax base for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year), from the global income tax base for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year;
  2. Where the person engaging in a small or medium enterprise is a domestic corporation: An amount calculated by subtracting the amount of item (b) from the amount of item (a):
    (a) An amount of corporate tax, as calculated for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year;
    (b) An amount calculated by applying the tax rate for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year to the amount calculated by subtracting losses incurred in the taxable year in which December 31, 2021 falls and defined in Article 14 (2) of the Corporate Tax Act, for which the person wishes to be granted a retroactive tax credit (limited to the tax base for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year), from the tax base for the immediately preceding taxable year or the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year;
  (2) Where a retroactive tax credit is granted for losses under Article 8-4 of the Act, if there are amounts payable for income tax or corporate tax on the small or medium enterprise for the immediately preceding taxable year and the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year respectively, the losses shall be deducted first from the tax base of income tax or corporate tax on business income for the taxable year before the immediately preceding taxable year. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (3) A person who wishes to receive a refund of an amount for which a retroactive tax credit on losses is granted under Article 8-4 of the Act shall submit an application for special tax refund following retroactive tax credit for losses with the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, within the period set for filing a final return on the tax base under Article 70, 70-2 or 74 of the Income Tax Act or the period set for filing a tax return under Article 60 of the Corporate Tax Act. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (4) Deleted. <Feb. 15, 2022>
  (5) Deleted. <Feb. 15, 2022>
  (6) Deleted. <Feb. 15, 2022>
