SECTION 2 Special Taxation for Research and Human Resources Development

Article 8 Deleted. <Feb. 11, 2020>

Article 9 (Tax Credits for Research and Human Resources Development Expenses) (1)"Expenses specified by Presidential Decree" in the former part of the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 10 (1) of the Act means the expenses listed in attached Table 6 as expenses for research and development and human resources development: Provided, the following expenses shall be excluded herefrom: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. Amount spent for research and development expenses from contributions, etc. received for research and development under Article 10-2 (1) of the Act;
  2. Amounts spent for research and development expenses or human resource development expenses from assets, such as contributions received from the State, local governments, public institutions under the Act on the Management of Public Institutions, and local public enterprises under the Local Public Enterprises Act.
  (2)"Technologies specified by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the items, of Article 10 (1) 1 of the Act means the technologies listed on attached Table 7 (hereinafter referred to as"new growth or source technologies"). <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (3) Research and development expenses incurred in acquiring new growth or source technologies under the provisions, with the exception of the items, of Article 10 (1) 1 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as"research and development expenses for new growth or source technologies") means the following expenses: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15. 2022>
  1. In cases of in-house research and development: The following expenses:
    (a) Personnel expenses for researchers engaging in research and development of new growth and source technologies (hereafter in this Article referred to as"research and development of new growth and source technologies") at any of the research institutes or specialized departments prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and for persons who directly support research and development of such researchers: Provided, That personnel expenses for persons prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance shall be excluded herefrom;
    (b) Expenses incurred in purchasing samples, parts, raw materials, and reagents used for research and development of new growth or source technologies, and expenses incurred in borrowing and purchasing software (limited to the software used for the purpose of manufacturing cultural products defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Framework Act on the Promotion of Cultural Industries), fonts, sound sources, and images;
  2. In cases of outsourced or joint research and development: Expenses incurred in outsourcing (including re-outsourcing) research and development of new growth or source technologies to any of the institutions prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (excluding expenses incurred in outsourcing the development of systems related to the operation, management and support of business operations of an enterprise, such as enterprise resource management facilities and point of sale information management system facilities) and expenses incurred in conducting joint research and development with any of such institutions.
  (4)"Middle-standing enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (1) 1 (a) (ii) of the Act means any enterprise that meets each of the following requirements: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2013; Nov. 29, 2013; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020, Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. That It shall not be a small or medium enterprise;
  1-2. That it shall not be an institution defined in Article 2 (1) 1 or 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on the Promotion of Growth and the Strengthening of Competitiveness of Middle-Standing Enterprises;
  2. That it shall not operate any of the following business as its principal business. In such cases, if it engages in two or more different businesses, the business generating more revenue shall be deemed its principal business:
    (a) Consumer service business under Article 29 (3);
    (b) A line of business referred to in any item of Article 2 (2) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on the Promotion of Growth and the Strengthening of Competitiveness of Middle-Standing Enterprises;
  3. That substantial independence between ownership and management shall meet the criteria under Article 2 (2) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Special Act on the Promotion of Growth and the Strengthening of Competitiveness of Middle-Standing Enterprises;
  4. That the average turnover for the immediately preceding three taxable years (turnover shall be calculated by the formula prescribed in Article 2 (4); if a taxable period is less one year, the turnover for such period shall be converted for one year) shall be less than 500 billion won.
  (5)"Multiplying factor prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 10 (1) 1 (b) and Article 10 (1) 2 (b) of the Act means three times. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (6)"Technologies prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the items, of Article 10 (1) 2 of the Act means the technologies listed on attached Table 7-2 (hereinafter referred to as"national strategic technologies"). <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (7) The research and development expenses for national strategic technologies under the provisions, with the exception of the items, of Article 10 (1) 2 of the Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as" research and development expenses for national strategic technologies") means the following expenses: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. In cases of in-house research and development: The following expenses:
    (a) Personnel expenses for researchers engaging in research and development of national strategic technologies (hereafter in this Article referred to as"research and development of national strategic technologies") at any of the research institutes or specialized departments prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and for persons who directly support research and development of such researchers: Provided, That personnel expenses for persons prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance shall be excluded herefrom;
    (b) Expenses incurred in purchasing samples, parts, raw materials, and reagents used for the research and development of national strategic technologies;
  2. In cases of outsourced or joint research and development: Expenses incurred in outsourcing (including re-outsourcing) research and development of national strategic technologies to any of the institutions prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (excluding expenses incurred in outsourcing the development of systems related to the operation, management and support of business operations of an enterprise, such as enterprise resource management facilities and point of sale information management system facilities) and expenses incurred in conducting joint research and development with any of such institutions.
  (8)"Where a small or medium enterprise first ceases to be a small or medium enterprise, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (1) 3 (b) of the Act means where the taxable year during which the ground making the small or medium enterprise cease to be a small or medium enterprise arises and the three subsequent taxable years thereafter elapse pursuant to the main clause of Article 2 (2), with the exception of its subparagraphs, and Article 2 (5). <Newly Inserted on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (9) The annual average of general research and human resources development expenses incurred for the four years prescribed in Article 10 (2) of the Act shall be calculated by the following formula: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (Aggregate of general research and human resources development expenses incurred for the four years retrospectively from the date the relevant taxable year commences ÷ Number of taxable years in which the general research and human resources development expenses incurred for the four years retrospectively from the date the relevant taxable year commences (four, if such number exceeds four)) × (Number of months in the relevant taxable year ÷ 12)
  (10) When calculating the aggregate of general research and human resources development expenses incurred in the immediately preceding taxable year under Article 10 (1) 3 of the Act and general research and human resources development expenses incurred during the four years retrospectively from the date the relevant taxable year commences in the formula described in paragraph (9), the general research and human resources development expenses incurred by a merged corporation, a divided corporation, a business transferor, or an investor in kind (hereafter in this paragraph, referred to as “merged corporation, etc.”) before a merger, a split-off, a merger by division, a transfer of business, or an investment in kind in the manner prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (hereafter in this paragraph, referred to as "merger, etc."), shall be deemed to have incurred by the merging corporation, the corporation newly incorporated in the course of the split-off, the counterpart corporation to the merger by division, the business transferee, or the corporation that receives the investment in kind in the manner prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (hereafter in this paragraph, referred to as "merging corporation, etc."): Provided, That, if it is impracticable to separate the general research and human resources development expenses incurred by the merged corporation, etc. in connection with the transferred business before the merger, etc., where the business operated by the merged corporation, etc. is partially transferred, the amount calculated by multiplying the general research and human resources development expenses incurred by the merged corporation, etc. by the greater of the ratio of the turnover of the transferred business for each business year to the total turnover, and the ratio of the value of assets of the transferred business as at the end of each business year to the total assets, shall be deemed the general research and human resources development expenses incurred by the merged corporation, etc. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (11) For the purposes of the formula described in paragraph (9), the number of months shall be calculated on the basis of calendar months, and if the number of days in the month during which a taxable year commences, is less than one full month, it shall be deemed one month, while the month during which a taxable year ends shall be disregarded in counting the number of months, if the number of days in that month is less than one full month. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (12) A national who wishes to be eligible under Article 10 (1) 1 or 2 of the Act shall keep separate accounts for research and development expenses for new growth or source technologies, research and development expenses for national strategic technologies, and general research and human resource development expenses. If the research and development expenses for new growth or source technologies, the research and development expenses for national strategic technologies, and the general research and human resource development expenses are overlapped, the relevant expenses shall be calculated by dividing proportionally into the research and development expenses for new growth or source technologies, the research and development expenses for national strategic technologies, and the general research and human resource development expenses, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (13) A national who wishes to be eligible under Article 10 (1) of the Act shall prepare and keep evidentiary documents, including a research and development plan, a research and development reports, and research notes, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (14) A national who wishes to be eligible under Article 10 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax credits, a statement of research and human resources development expenses, and evidentiary documents, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, at the time he/she files a tax return. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (15) A deliberative committee on technologies eligible for tax credits on research and development shall be established under the joint jurisdiction of the Minister of Economy and Finance and the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy to deliberate on the following matters: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Whether a technology for which a national conducts research and development is classifiable as national strategic technology;
  2. Matters concerning the recognition of facilities for the commercialization of new growth engines under Article 21 (4) 1 (a);
  3. Matters concerning the recognition of facilities for the commercialization of national strategic technologies under Article 21 (4) 2;
  4. Other matters recognized by the Minister of Economy and Finance or the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy as those on which deliberation is necessary in relation to new growth engines or source technologies or national strategic technologies.
  (16) The composition and operation of the deliberative committee on technologies eligible for tax credits on research and development under paragraph (15) and other necessary matters shall be prescribed by Joint Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (17) A national who wishes to be eligible under Article 10 (1) of the Act may request the Commissioner of the National Tax Service to examine in advance whether the expenses he/she has spent qualify as research and human resources development expenses, before he/she files a tax return under paragraph (14). In such cases, examination methods and matters necessary for requesting procedures, etc. shall be determined by the Commissioner of the National Tax Service. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (18)"Ground prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the cases referred to in subparagraphs of Article 14-3 of the Basic Research Promotion and Technology Development Support Act" in Article 10 (6) of the Act means any of the following cases: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Where the recognition of a business-related research institute or a department exclusively dedidated to research and development is revoked on any of the grounds prescribed in Article 14-3 (1) of the Basic Research Promotion and Technology Development Support Act;
  2. Where the recognition of a business-affiliated creative research institute or a department solely responsible for creation in a company is revoked on any of the grounds prescribed in Article 17-3 (4) of the Framework Act on the Promotion of Cultural Industries.
  (19)"Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10 (6) of the Act means the day specified in any of the following subparagraphs for the ground for revocation of recognition under each subparagraph of paragraph (18): <Newly Inserted on Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Where recognition is revoked under Article 14-3 (1) 1 of the Basic Research Promotion and Technology Development Support Act or Article 17-3 (4) 1 of the Framework Act on the Promotion of Cultural Industries: The beginning date of the taxable year in which recognition was granted;
  2. Where recognition is revoked under Article 14-3 (1) 2, 3, 5, 6, or 8 of the Basic Research Promotion and Technology Development Support Act: The date recognition is revoked.
  3. Where recognition is revoked under Article 14-3 (1) 4 or 7 of the Basic Research Promotion and Technology Development Support Act or Article 17-3 (4) 2 of the Framework Act on the Promotion of Cultural Industries: The beginning date of the taxable year in which recognition is revoked.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Feb. 18, 2010]

Article 9-2 (Special Taxation on Contributions Related to Research and Development) (1)"Act prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10-2 (1) of the Act means any of the following Acts: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Aug. 18, 2009; Feb. 18, 2010>
