  2. Real estate leasing and supply business.
  (2)"Assets prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provision of Article 24 (1) 1 (b) of the Act means assets prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, such as land and buildings.
  (3)"Assets prescribed by Presidential Decree, among tangible and intangible assets not falling under item (a)" in Article 24 (1) 1 (b) of the Act means the following assets: <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Assets prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, among business assets used for research and testing, vocational training, energy saving, environmental conservation, or employees’ welfare;
  2. assets prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, such as vehicles and carriers used directly by a person engaged in a transportation business for the business;
  3. The following assets acquired by a small or medium enterprise (excluding assets acquired from a related party pursuant to Article 11 (1));
    (a) A patent established and registered first under the Patent Act for research and development by a national in the Republic of Korea;
    (b) A utility model right established and registered first under the Utility Model Act for research and development by a national in the Republic of Korea;
    (c) A design right established and registered first under the Design Protection Act for research and development by a national in the Republic of Korea;
  (4)"Facility prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 24 (1) 2 (a) (i) and (ii) means any of the following facilities: <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Facilities under Article 24 (1) 2 (a) (i) of the Act: The following facilities:
    (a) A facility jointly recognized by the Minister of Economy and Finance and the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy after deliberation by the deliberative committee for technologies eligible for tax credits on research and development as a facility for commercializing new growth and source technologies (including facilities used for the production of products other than products produced using new growth and source technologies) as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (hereinafter referred to as"facility for commercialization of new growth engines");
    (b) A facility for switching, transmission, or power supply under subparagraph 6 (a) (i) or (ii) of attached Table 7, among telecommunications facilities under Article 8 of the Regulations on Accounting and Reporting of Telecommunications Business, which are necessary for the operation of fifth-generation mobile communications base stations (including switching facilities interconnected therewith) equipped with the technologies in items (i) and (ii) of that subparagraph;
  2. Facilities under Article 24 (1) 2 (a) (ii) of the Act: Facilities jointly recognized by the Minister of Economy and Finance and the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy after deliberation by the deliberative committee for technologies eligible for tax credits on research and development, among facilities for commercializing national strategic technologies (including facilities used for the production of products other than the products produced using national strategic technologies) as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance (hereinafter referred to as"facilities for commercialization of national strategic technologies")
  (5)"Period prescribed by presidential decree" in the former part of Article 24 (3) of the Act means the period prescribed in any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. For a building or structure prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance as a business asset falling under any subparagraph of paragraph (3): Five years;
  2. For a facility for commercialization of new growth engines or national strategic technologies, which is used also for the production of products other than those produced using the technology: The period until the end of three subsequent taxable years after the taxable year in which investments are completed;
  3. For a business asset other than the assets under items 1 and 2: Two years.
  (6)"Additional amount equivalent to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 24 (3) of the Act shall be calculated by multiplying the deducted amount by the period specified in subparagraph 1 and the rate specified in subparagraph 2. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. The period from the date following the filing date of the tax return for the tax-deducted taxable year to the filing date of the tax return for the taxable year in which the ground specified in Article 24 (3) of the Act arises;
  2. The rate specified in Article 11-2 (9) 2.
  (7) An investment amount under Article 24 (1) and (2) of the Act shall be calculated by subtracting the amount specified in subparagraph 2 from the amount specified in subparagraph 1:
  1. An amount calculated according to the work progress rate under Article 69 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act or the amount actually disbursed until the relevant taxable year, whichever is greater;
  2. The aggregate of the following amounts:
    (a) Investment amount to which Article 24 of the Act was applied before the relevant taxable year;
    (b) The amount calculated by applying mutatis mutandis subparagraph 1 to the portion invested before the relevant taxable year, except the amount of item (a).
  (8) The average annual investment amount for three years under Article 24 (1) 2 (b) and 3 (b) shall be calculated according to the following formula: In such cases, if the period from the beginning of the taxable year in which a national initially made an investment to the beginning of the taxable year in which the person wishes to be granted a tax credit thereon is less than 36 months, an amount calculated by converting the aggregate of the amounts invested in that period into 36 months shall be deemed the amount invested for three years retroactively from the beginning of the relevant taxable year; and if the national is a merging corporation, a corporation established after a division, a counter-party corporation of a merge through a division, a corporation that acquired a business, or a corporation that received an investment in kind (hereafter in this paragraph referred to as"a merging corporation or the like"), the amount invested by the merged corporation, divided corporation, the person that transferred the business, or the person who made the investment in kind shall be deemed to have been invested by the merging corporation or the like: <Amended on Feb. 28, 2023; Jun. 7, 2023>
  Aggregate of amounts invested for three years retroactively from the beginning of the relevant taxable year/3 × Number of months of the relevant taxable year/12
  (9) For the purposes of Article 24 (1) 2 (b) and 3 (b) of the Act, if there is no average annual investment amount calculated for three years according to paragraph (8), there is no amount eligible for additional deduction. <Amended on Jun. 7, 2023>
  (10) For the purposes of Article 24 (3) of the Act, if a facility under paragraph (5) 2 falls under any of the following subparagraphs, such facility shall be deemed to have been diverted to another purpose at the end of the period specified in that paragraph: Provided, That such facility shall not be deemed to have been diverted to another purpose if the facility has been extinguished by a natural disaster or there is any other ground prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. In cases of a facility for commercialization of new growth engines: Where the ratio of the aggregate of the output of products produced using new growth or source technologies and the output of products produced using national strategic technologies to the total output of all products produced at the facility during the period from the date of completion of investments (referring to April 1, 2022 if the date of completion of investments is prior to April 1, 2022) to the date specified in paragraph (5) 2 is not more than 50/100;
  2. In cases of a facility for commercialization of national strategic technologies: Where the ratio of the aggregate of the output of products produced using national strategic technologies to the total output of all products produced at the facility during the period from the date of completion of investments (referring to April 1, 2022 if the date of completion of investments is prior to April 1, 2022) to the date specified in paragraph (5) 2 is not more than 50/100;
  (11) Where a facility for commercialization of new growth engines or national strategic technologies is deemed to have been diverted to another purpose under paragraph (10), the" amount equivalent to the tax credit amount so granted" under the former part of Article 24 (3) of the Act shall be calculated according to the following subparagraphs: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. In cases of a facility for commercialization of new growth engines: The amount of the tax credit granted minus the amount of the tax credit entitled to be granted if the facility is not a facility for commercialization of new growth engines or national strategic technologies (hereafter in this paragraph referred to as a"general facility");
  2. In cases of a facility for commercialization of national strategic technologies: The amount of the tax credit granted minus the amount of the tax credit entitled to be granted if the facility is a general facility (or the amount of the tax credit entitled to be granted as a facility for commercialization of new growth engines if the ratio of the aggregate of the output of products produced using new growth or source technologies and the output of products produced using national strategic technologies to the total output of all products produced at the facility, if the facility is a general facility, exceeds 50/100).
  (12) For the purposes of paragraphs (1) through (11), Article 23 (14) shall apply mutatis mutandis with respect to the timing of commencement of investments. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (13) A person who wishes to be granted a tax credit pursuant to Article 24 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for the tax credit in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with the tax return for the relevant taxable year. In such cases, the tax credit may be applied for as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance before the facility is recognized as a facility for commercialization of new growth engines or national strategic technologies under the condition that it shall be recognized as such facility. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (14) A person who wishes to be granted a tax credit pursuant to Article 24 (1) of the Act for a facility used also for the production of products other than those produced using new growth engines or national strategic technologies, among facilities for commercialization of new growth engines or national strategic technologies, shall measure the volume of all products produced in that facility and keep records of the production volume, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and shall submit the data about the actual production volume in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, when filing the tax return for the last taxable year of the period specified in Paragraph (5) 2. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
