  2. Where the number of full-time employees or full-time youth employees, etc., decreases from the number of full-time employees in the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted under Article 29-7 (1) of the Act during the period beginning on the day following the period under subparagraph 1 and ending at the end of the taxable year in which the second anniversary of the end of the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted: An amount calculated as follows (excluding the amount calculated under subparagraph 1, if any, and limited to the total amount of the tax deducted under Article 29-7 (1) of the Act in the taxable years within two years immediately preceding the relevant taxable year):
    (a) Where the number of full-time employees decreases: An amount calculated as follows:
    (i) Where the reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc. is not less than the reduced number of full-time employees:
  An amount calculated according to the following formula: [Increased number of full-time youth employees, as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc., during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted) ? Reduced number of full-time employees] × (Amount under Article 29-7 (1) 1 of the Act ? Amount under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph) + (Reduced number of full-time employees × Amount under Article 29-7 (1) 1 of the Act)
    (ii) In other cases: The aggregate of tax amounts deducted in the taxable years within two immediately preceding years for the decrease in the number of full-time youth employees, etc. and full-time employees other than full-time youth employees, etc. (limited to the decrease in the number of full-time employees), as compared to the number in the taxable year in which the deduction was first made;
