  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 13, 2018]

Article 26-8 (Integrated Tax Credit for Employment) (1)"Types of business prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as a consumer service business" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 29-8 (1) of the Act means the consumer service business under Article 29 (3).
  (2)"Full-time employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 29-8 (1) of the Act means the full-time employees under Article 23 (10) (hereafter in this Article referred to as"full-time employees").
  (3)"Full-time employees prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as regular youth employees, employees with disabilities, and employees aged 60 or older" in Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act means any of the following persons among full-time employees (hereafter in this Article referred to as"full-time youth employees, etc.):
  1. Persons aged between 15 and 34 years (referring to the age calculated by deducting the period of military service of not more than six years from the present age if the relevant employees have completed military service under any item of Article 27 (1) 1, excluding any of the following persons:
    (a) Fixed-term employees and part-time employees defined in the Act on the Protection of Fixed-Term and Part-Time Employees;
    (b) Temporary agency workers under the Act on the Protection of Temporary Agency Workers;
    (c) Youth defined in the Youth Protection Act and working in any place designated pursuant to that Act as harmful to youth;
  2. Persons with disabilities eligible under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities; wounded persons under the Act on the Honorable Treatment of and Support for Persons of Distinguished Service to the State; persons wounded during their participation under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service to the May 18 Democratization Movement and Establishment of Related Organizations; and persons having received disability ratings as patients suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants defined in the Act on Assistance to Patients Suffering from Actual or Potential Aftereffects of Defoliants and Establishment of Related Organizations;
  3. Persons aged 60 or older as at the date of conclusion of an employment contract;
  4. Carrier-interrupted women under Article 29-3 (1) of the Act.
  (4) The amount of income tax or corporate tax payable under the latter part of 29-8 (2) of the Act shall be calculated as follows and shall be paid as income tax or corporate tax at the time of filing a tax return for the relevant taxable year.
  1. Where the number of all full-time employees or the number of full-time youth employees, etc. decreases, as compared to the number in the taxable year in which the deduction was first made under Article 29-8 (1) of the Act during the period beginning at the end of the taxable year in which the deduction was first made and ending at the end of the taxable year in which the first anniversary of the end of the taxable year in which the deduction was first made falls: An amount calculated as follows (limited to the amount of tax deducted under Article 29-8 (1) of the Act for the taxable year within one year immediately preceding the relevant taxable year);
    (a) Where the number of all full-time employee decreases: An amount calculated as follows:
    (i) Where the reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc. is not less than the reduced number of all full-time employees: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  [Reduced number of full-time youth employees, as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc., during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted) ? Reduced number of all full-time employees] × (Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act ? Amount under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph) × Number of deductions for taxable years within immediately preceding two years +(Reduced number of all full-time employees × Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act × Number of deductions for taxable years within immediately preceding two years)
    (ii) In other cases: An amount calculated by the following formula:
  [Reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc., as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the reduced number of full-time employees) × (Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act)] + [Reduced number of full-time employees other than full-time youth employees, etc., as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the reduced number of full-time employees) × Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 2 of the Act]
    (b) Where the number of full-time employees does not decrease but the number of full-time youth employees, etc., decreases: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  Reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc., as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc. during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted) × (Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act - Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 2 of the Act)
  2. Where the number of full-time employees or full-time youth employees, etc., decreases from the number of full-time employees in the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted under Article 29-8 (1) of the Act during the period beginning on the day following the period under subparagraph 1 and ending at the end of the taxable year in which the second anniversary of the end of the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted: An amount calculated as follows (excluding the amount calculated under subparagraph 1, if any, and limited to the total amount of the tax deducted under Article 29-8 (1) of the Act in the taxable years within two years immediately preceding the relevant taxable year):
    (a) Where the number of all full-time employee decreases: An amount calculated as follows:
    (i) Where the reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc. is not less than the reduced number of all full-time employees: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  [Reduced number of full-time youth employees, as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc., during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted) ? Reduced number of all full-time employees] × (Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act ? Amount under subparagraph 2 of that paragraph) × Number of deductions for taxable years within immediately preceding two years +(Reduced number of all full-time employees × Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act × Number of deductions for taxable years within immediately preceding two years)
    (ii) In other cases: The aggregate of tax amounts deducted in taxable years within two immediately preceding years for the decrease in the number of full-time youth employees, etc. and full-time employees other than full-time youth employees, etc. (limited to the decrease in the number of full-time employees), as compared to the number in the taxable year in which the deduction was first made;
    (b) Where the number of full-time employees does not decrease but the number of full-time youth employees, etc., decreases: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  Reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc., as compared to the number during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc. during the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted) × (Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 1 of the Act - Amount under Article 29-8 (1) 2 of the Act)
  (5) For the purposes of paragraph (4), persons classified as full-time youth employees, etc. under paragraph (3) 1 for the taxable year in which the tax was first deducted shall be deemed full-time youth employees, etc. for subsequent taxable years thereafter in counting the number of full-time youth employees, etc.
  (6) For the purposes of Article 29-8 (1) through (4) of the Act, the number of full-time employees and the number of full-time youth employees shall be calculated by the following applicable formulas (a fraction of less than 1/100 shall be deemed nil).
  1. The number of full-time employees:
  Aggregate of the number of full-time employees as at the end of each month in the relevant taxable year ÷ Number of months in the relevant taxable year
  2. The number of full-time youth employees, etc.:
  Aggregate of the number of full-time youth employees, etc. as at the end of each month in the relevant taxable year ÷ Number of months in the relevant taxable year
  (7) The latter part of Article 23 (11) shall apply to the calculation of the number of full-time workers and young full-time workers pursuant to paragraph (6), and when applying Article 29-8 (3) and (4) of the Act, if there is a full-time worker who replaces a full-time worker on maternity leave pursuant to Article 74 of the Labor Standards Act, the full-time worker who is on maternity leave shall be excluded from the number of full-time workers and young full-time workers pursuant to paragraph (6). <Amended on Feb. 29, 2024>
  (8) For the purposes of paragraph (6), Article 23 (13) shall apply mutatis mutandis to a national who commences a business, etc. in the relevant taxable year. In such cases, "the number of full-time employees" shall be construed as "the number of full-time employees or the number of full-time youth employees, etc."
  (9)"Special relationship prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 29-8 (3) and Article 29-8 (4) 3 of the Act means kinship under Article 1-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes.
  (10) Whether or not earned income tax for a returnee from childcare leave has been withheld by an enterprise pursuant to Article 29-8 (4) 1 of the Act shall be verified by the book for tax withholding for earned income under Article 196 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act.
  (11) A person who wishes to be granted a tax credit under Article 29-8 (1), (3) or (4) of the Act shall submit an application for the tax credit and a statement of the amount of the tax credit, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment when filing a tax return.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 28, 2023]

Article 27 (Income Tax Reduction or Exemption for Employees of Small or Medium Enterprises) (1)"Youth prescribed by Presidential Decree, a person aged 60 or older, a person with a disability, or a career-interrupted woman" in the former part of Article 30 (1) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Nov. 20, 2015; Nov. 29, 2016; Feb. 7, 2017; Aug. 28, 2018; Feb. 12, 2019>
  1. Youth: A person aged between 15 and 34 years as at the conclusion date of an employment contract: Provided, That persons whose age calculated by deducting the period of military service from the present age does not exceed 34 shall be included therein if such persons have completed military service that falls under any of the following items:
    (a) Active duty servicemen under Article 16 or 20 of the Military Service Act (including full-time reserve servicemen, auxiliary police officers, and obligatory firefighters who completed their service under Articles 21 and 25 of that Act);
    (b) Social service personnel under Article 26 (1) of the Military Service Act;
    (c) Officers, warrant officers, and noncommissioned officers under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Military Personnel Management Act;
  2. A person aged 60 or older: A person aged 60 or older as at the conclusion date of an employment contract;
  3. A person with a disability: Any of the following persons:
    (a) Persons eligible under the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
    (b) Wounded persons defined in the Act on the Honorable Treatment of and Support for Persons of Distinguished Service to the State;
    (c) Persons wounded in the May 18 Democratization Movement, as defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 4 of the Act on the Honorable Treatment of Persons of Distinguished Service to the May 18 Democratization Movement and Establishment of Related Organizations;
    (d) Persons having received disability ratings as patients suffering from potential aftereffects of defoliants defined in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act on Assistance to Patients Suffering from Actual or Potential Aftereffects of Defoliants and Establishment of Related Organizations;
  4. Carrier-interrupted women: Carrier-interrupted women under Article 29-3 (1) of the Act.
  (2) The following persons shall be disregarded for the purposes of paragraph (1): <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012; Aug 31, 2012; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 12, 2019>
  1. Executive officers specified under subparagraphs of Article 40 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act;
  2. The largest stockholder or the largest investor of the relevant enterprise (referring to the representative, if the relevant enterprise is a sole proprietorship), and his/her spouse;
  3. Lineal ascendants and descendants (including their spouses) of the persons referred to in subparagraph 2, and relatives defined in Article 1-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes, of such persons;
  4. Daily employed workers defined in Article 14 (3) 2 of the Income Tax Act;
  5. Persons regarding whom it is not confirmed whether they have ever paid either of the following: Provided, That excluded herefrom are the persons who are not eligible to be insured under the National Pension Scheme under the proviso to Article 6 of the National Pension Act and the persons who are not eligible for the coverage of the National Health Insurance under the proviso to Article 5 (1) of the National Health Insurance Act:
    (a) An employer contribution or employee endowment defined in Article 3 (1) 11 or 12 of the National Pension Act;
    (b) Premiums of employer-provided policy-holders under Article 69 of the National Health Insurance Act.
  (3) "Enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30 (1) of the Act means an enterprise mainly engaging in any of the following businesses: Provided, That the State, local governments (including associations of local governments), public institutions under the Act on the Management of Public Institutions, and local public enterprises under the Local Public Enterprises Act shall be excluded herefrom: <Amended on Feb. 11. 2020; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Agriculture, forestry, and fisheries;
  2. Mining;
  3. Manufacturing;
  4. Electricity, gas, steam, and water supply;
  5. Waterworks, sewage and waste disposal, and raw material recycling business;
  6. Construction;
  7. Wholesale and retail businesses;
  8. Storage and warehousing business;
  9. Lodging and restaurant business (excluding pubs and non-alcoholic beverage shops);
  10. Information and communications service business (excluding business operating rooms for viewing video products);
  11. Real estate business;
  12. Research and development business;
  13. Advertising business;
  14. Market research and opinion survey business;
  15. Architectural technology, engineering, and other scientific and technological service business;
  16. Other specialized, scientific, and technological service business;
  17. Business facility management, business support and rental service business;
  18. Technical and occupational training institutes;
  18-2. Computer academy;
  19. Social welfare service business;
  20. Maintenance and repair services for personal and consumer goods;
  21. Creative or art-related service business;
  22. Libraries, historical sites, and similar service business related to leisure;
  23. Sport service business.
  (4)"Military service prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30 (1) of the Act means any military service prescribed under paragraph (1) 1. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2015>
  (5) A worker who intends to apply for a reduction of income tax under Article 30 (2) of the Act shall file an application for tax reduction, in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the withholding agent, along with a document, etc. evidencing the period of military service, by no later than the end of the month immediately following the month in which the date of employment falls. In such cases, the withholding agent may withhold income tax on earned income for each month by applying the reduction or exemption rate specified in Article 30 (1) of the Act, notwithstanding Article 134 (1) of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016>
  (6) A withholding agent shall also submit a statement of the persons eligible for tax red+P9191:P9194uction, in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, when submitting a list of employees who have applied for tax reduction under Article 30 (3) of the Act to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the withholding. <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 3, 2015>
  (7) A withholding agent shall submit a statement of retirees ineligible for tax reduction in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, when notifying the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the withholding of the fact that an employee has resigned under the proviso of Article 30 (5) of the Act. <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 3, 2015>
  (8) Where a person has earned income paid by a small or medium enterprise under Article 30 (1) of the Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as"tax-exempted or reduced income") and other global income, the amount of tax to be exempted or reduced for the relevant taxable period shall be calculated by the following formula, subject to a ceiling of two million won for each taxable period: <Amended on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 28, 2023>
  Reduced or exempted amount of tax = A × (B/C) × (D/E) × F
  A: Tax amount calculated on global income under Article 55 (1) of the Income Tax Act
  B: Amount of earned income under Article 20 (2) of the Income Tax Act
  C: Amount of global income under Article 14 (2) of the Income Tax Act D: Gross salary received from a small or medium enterprise under Article 30 (1) of the Act E: Gross salary of the relevant employee F: Reduction rate under Article 30 (1) of the Act
  (9) For the purpose of granting a tax credit on earned income under Article 59 (1) of the Income Tax Act, if a person has tax-exempted or reduced income and other earned income (including cases where a person has no earned income in addition to tax-exempted or reduced income), the amount calculated by the following formula shall be determined as the amount of the tax credit on earned income: <Amended on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 17, 2021>
  Amount of tax credit on earned income = A × [1 ? (B/C)]
  A: Amount of tax credit on earned income as calculated pursuant to Article 59 (1) of the Income Tax Act
  B: Reduced or exempted amount of tax
  C: Tax amount calculated on global income under Article 55 (1) of the Income Tax Act × (Amount of earned income under Article 20 (2) of the Income Tax Act/Amount of global income under Article 14 (2) of the Income Tax Act)
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Mar. 26, 2010]
  [Title Amended on Feb. 21, 2014]

Article 27-2 Deleted. <Feb. 28, 2023>

Article 27-3 (Special Taxation for Small or Medium Enterprises Maintaining Employment) (1) The hourly rate of a full-time employee in the immediately preceding taxable year or the relevant taxable year referred to in Article 30-3 (1) 1 and (2) 2 of the Act (excluding full-time employees who enter into an employment contract in the relevant taxable year; hereafter in this paragraph and paragraph (5), the same shall apply), shall be calculated by dividing the total wages referred to in subparagraph 1 by the total working hours referred to in subparagraph 2: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019>
  1. Total wages: The aggregate of ordinary wages and the amount of fixed payments, such as regular bonuses, paid to full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year or the relevant taxable year;
  2. Total working hours: Total working hours stipulated in the employment contracts of full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year or the relevant taxable year (or total actual working hours in cases of a part-time worker defined in Article 2 (1) 9 of the Labor Standards Act, who works for at least 60 hours for one month).
  (2)"Rate prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-3 (1) 2 of the Act means 0/100.
  (3) A small or medium enterprise which intends to be accorded special taxation for maintaining employment pursuant to Article 30-3 of the Act shall file an application for tax credits in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, accompanied by the documents verifying an agreement between the business operator and the employees' representative, with the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with its tax return for income tax or corporate tax. <Amended on Jun. 19, 2009; Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 12, 2019>
  (4) For the purposes of Article 30-3 (1) through (3) of the Act, the full-time employees mean workers who enter into an employment contract under the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That the following persons shall be excluded herefrom: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012; Aug 31, 2012; Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 12, 2019; Jun. 2, 2020>
  1. Any person whose employment contract is for less than one year: Provided, That for the purposes of Article 30-3 (3) of the Act, an employee whose employment contract is not less than one year in total as a consequence of consecutive renewal of the employment contract shall be deemed a full-time employee;
  2. Executive officers specified under subparagraphs of Article 40 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act;
  3. The largest stockholder or the largest investor of the relevant enterprise (referring to the representative, if the relevant enterprise is a sole proprietorship), and his/her spouse;
  4. Lineal ascendants and descendants of the persons referred to in subparagraph 3 and their spouses;
  5. Persons regarding whom it is not verified by the book for tax withholding for earned income under Article 196 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act whether or not income tax on earned income has been withheld and whether or not insurance premiums. etc. falling under any of the following have been paid:
    (a) An employer contribution or employee endowment defined in Article 3 (1) 11 or 12 of the National Pension Act;
    (b) Premiums of employer-provided policy-holders under Article 69 of the National Health Insurance Act.
  6. A part-time employee defined in Article 2 (1) 9 of the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That an employee whose contractual work hours per month are at least 60 hours shall be deemed a full-time employee.
  (5) For the purposes of Article 30-3 (1) 3 and (2) of the Act, the total annual wages per full-time employee of the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, shall be calculated by dividing the total wages prescribed in subparagraph 1 by the number of full-time employees calculated by the formula prescribed in subparagraph 2: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012>
  1. Total wages: The aggregate of ordinary wages and the amount of fixed payments, such as regular bonuses, paid to full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year or the relevant taxable year;
  2. The number of full-time employees:
  Aggregate of the number of full-time employees as at the end of each month in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year ÷ Number of months in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year
  (6) Where the number of full-time employees has reduced because the labor relationship is terminated due to a death, mandatory retirement, or other similar reasons in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, the reduced number of employees shall be disregarded for the purposes of calculating the number of full-time employees and the total annual wages per full-time employee under paragraph (5), deeming that they did not work from the immediately preceding taxable year. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012>
  (7) Where full-time employees who have worked in the previous business division are succeeded due to a merger, general acquisition of a business, or any similar event in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, the number of persons succeeded shall be included in the number of full-time employees and the total annual wages per full-time employee under paragraph (5), deeming that they have worked for the succeeding enterprise from the immediately preceding taxable year. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012>
  (8) Where the number of full-time employees has reduced due to a split-off, general transfer of a business, or any similar event in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, the reduced number of employees shall be disregarded for the purposes of calculating the number of full-time employees and the total annual wages per full-time employee under paragraph (5), deeming that they did not work for an enterprise, etc. which is split-off or generally transferred, from the immediately preceding taxable year. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012>
  (9) The total working hours of all full-time employees for the relevant taxable year referred to in Article 30-3 (2) 2 of the Act shall be deemed the total working hours for the relevant taxable year provided for in paragraph (1) 2. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 7, 2017>
  (10) The total annual wages referred to in Article 30-3 (3) of the Act means the aggregate of ordinary wages and the amount of fixed payments, such as regular bonuses. In such cases, the total annual wages of a full-time employee whose labor relationship is established or terminated during the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, shall be calculated by the following applicable formula: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 7, 2017>
  1. The total annual wages of a full-time employee whose labor relationship was established in the immediately preceding taxable year in the relevant taxable year, shall be calculated by the following formula:
  Aggregate of ordinary wages and the amount of fixed payments in the relevant taxable year × (Total number of working days in the immediately preceding taxable year ÷ Total number of working days in the relevant taxable year)
  2. The total annual wages of a full-time employee whose labor relationship is terminated in the relevant taxable year in the immediately preceding taxable year, shall be calculated by the following formula:
  Aggregate of ordinary wages and the amount of fixed payments in the immediately preceding taxable year × (Total number of working days in the relevant taxable year ÷ Total number of working days in the immediately preceding taxable year)
  3. The total annual wages of a full-time employee whose labor relationship is succeeded due to a merger, split-off, etc. of an enterprise during the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, shall be the aggregate of wages paid by the previous employer, notwithstanding subparagraphs 1 and 2.
  (11)"Area prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-3 (5) 1 of the Act means an area designated and publicly notified by the Minister of Employment and Labor pursuant to Article 29 of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on Employment Policy. <Amended on Feb. 17, 2021>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Apr. 21, 2009]
  [Title Amended on Jun. 19, 2009]

Article 27-4 (Scope of Full-Time Employees in Granting Tax Credits for Social Insurance Premiums for Small or Medium Enterprises) (1) The full-time employees referred to in Article 30-4 (1) of the Act shall be the Korean workers who enter into an employment contract under the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That the following persons shall be excluded herefrom: <Amended on Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Jun. 2, 2020>
  1. An employee whose employment contract term is less than one year (excluding employees whose total employment contract term is not less than one year due to consecutive renewal of an employment contract);
  2. A part-time employee defined in Article 2 (1) 9 of the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That an employee whose contractual work hours per month are at least 60 hours shall be deemed a full-time employee;
  3. An executive officer falling under any subparagraph of Article 40 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act;
  4. The largest stockholder or the largest investor of the relevant enterprise (referring to the representative, if the relevant enterprise is a sole proprietorship), and his/her spouse;
  5. A lineal ascendant or descendant (including the spouses) of a person referred to in subparagraph 4 or a relative as defined in Article 1-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes, of such person;
  6. Persons regarding whom it is not confirmed whether income tax on earned income has ever been withheld by the book for tax withholding for earned income under Article 196 of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act;
  7. Employees regarding whom it is not confirmed whether contributions or premiums payable by their employers for the social insurance under Article 30-4 (4) of the Act have ever been paid.
  (2)"Youths and career-interrupted women hired as full-time employees" in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"youths, etc."), means the following persons; and"full-time employees, excluding youths, etc." in Article 30-4 (1) 2 of the Act means full-time employees who are not full-time youth employees, etc.: <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017>
  1. Full-time youth employees: Full-time employees between the ages of 15 and 29 (if a person has performed any military service specified under Article 27 (1) 1, and his age calculated by subtracting the period of such military service (which shall not exceed six years) from his age as on the date an employment contract is entered into, does not exceed 29 years, the person shall be deemed a youth);
  2. Career-interrupted women hired as full-time employees: Full-time employees who are career-interrupted women provided for in Article 29-3 (1) of the Act.
  (3)"Number of employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act means the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc. between the relevant taxable year and the immediately preceding taxable year (if the number is a negative, it shall be deemed zero): Provided, That its ceiling shall be the increased number of full-time employees in the relevant taxable year compared to the immediately preceding taxable year. <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017>
  (4)"Number of increased full-time employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (1) 2 of the Act means the increased number of full-time employees between the relevant taxable year and the immediately preceding taxable year (if the number is a negative, it shall be deemed zero) minus the number referred to in paragraph (3).
  (5)"Small or medium enterprise engaging in any of the new-growth service businesses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (1) 2 of the Act means a small or medium enterprise engaging mainly in any of the following business activities. In such cases, if it engages in two or more different businesses, the business generating more revenue shall be deemed its principal business: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 17, 2022>
  1. Computer programming, system integration and management services; software development and supply; information service activities; or telecommunications;
  2. Creative and arts-related services (excluding individual artists); business activities producing motion pictures, video, and broadcast programs; business activities of audio publishing and original master recording; or broadcasting;
  3. Engineering business; specialized designing services; security system service activities; or business making advertisements, among advertising businesses;
  4. Business publishing books, magazines, and other printed matters; research and development business; business operating a private institute teaching vocational skills under the Act on the Establishment and Operation of Private Teaching Institutes and Extracurricular Lessons; or business operating a vocational skill development training establishment under the National Lifelong Vocational Skills Development Act (limited to where the main business is vocational skill development training);
  5. Tourist accommodation business, international conference business, or amusement facility business under the Tourism Promotion Act; or tourist facilities business referred to in Article 6 (3) 20 of the Act;
  6. The logistics industry referred to in Article 5 (7);
  7. Other new-growth service businesses prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
  (6) For the purposes of granting a tax credit under Article 30-4 of the Act, the number of full-time employees and the number of full-time youth employees, etc. shall be calculated by the formulas prescribed in subparagraph 1: Provided, That one employee referred to in the proviso of paragraph (1) 2 shall be deemed 0.5 person for the purpose of calculation, but if all of the requirements for support under subparagraph 2 are met, one employee shall be deemed 0.75 person for the purpose of calculation, and a fraction of less than 1/100 shall be deemed nil: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Formulas for calculating the number of full-time employees and full-time youth employees, etc.:
    (a) Number of full-time employees:
  Aggregate of the number of full-time employees as at the end of each month during the relevant period ÷ Number of months during the relevant period
    (b) Number of full-time youth employees, etc.:
  Aggregate of the number of full-time youth employees, etc. as at the end of each month during the relevant period ÷ Number of months during the relevant period
  2. Requirements for support:
    (a) The number of full-time employees in the relevant taxable year (excluding the workers referred to in the proviso to paragraph (1) 2), shall not be smaller than that in the immediately preceding taxable year (excluding the workers referred to in the proviso to paragraph (1) 2);
    (b) They shall have entered into an indefinite employment contract;
    (c) They shall not be given discriminatory treatment defined in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act on the Protection of Fixed-Term and Part-Time Employees, in their hourly wages (including wages defined in Article 2 (1) 5 of the Labor Standards Act, regularly paid bonuses, such as regular bonuses and holiday bonuses, and performance-based incentives) and other matters concerning the terms and conditions of employment, welfare, etc., compared with the full-time employees;
    (d) The hourly wage shall be at least 120/100 of the minimum wage prescribed under Article 5 of the Minimum Wage Act.
  (7) When calculating the increased number of full-time youth employees, etc. or full-time employees referred to in paragraphs (3) and (4), the number classified as follows shall be deemed the number of full-time youth employees, etc. or the number of full-time employees in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year, if an enterprise starts its business, etc. in the relevant taxable year: <Amended on Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 12, 2019>
  1. Number of full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year where the national starts a business (excluding cases falling under Article 6 (10) 1 through 3 of the Act): 0;
  2. Number of full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year in cases falling under any of Article 6 (10) 1 (excluding succession to the previous business through a merger, a split-off, an investment in kind or acquisition of business) through 3 of the Act: Number of full-time youth employees, etc. or number of full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year of the previous business, business before conversion into a corporation, or business before closure of business;
  3. Number of full-time employees in the immediately preceding or relevant taxable year in either of the following cases: In cases of an enterprise that has transferred the business, the number calculated by deducting the number of full-time youth employees, etc. or the number of full-time employees transferred by succession from the number of full-time youth employees, etc. or the number of full-time employees in the immediately preceding taxable year; and in cases of an enterprise that has acquired the business, the aggregate of the number of full-time youth employees, etc. or the number of full-time employees by succession and the number of full-time youth employees, etc. or the number of full-time employees of an enterprise succeeded in the immediately preceding taxable year; and the number of full-time employees in the relevant taxable year shall be the number of full-time youth employees, etc. or the number of full-time employees calculated by deeming the full-time employees have been transferred or acquired by succession on the date the relevant taxable year commences:
    (a) Where such enterprise takes over full-time youth employees, etc. or full-time employees engaging in the previous business division due to a merger, a split-off, an investment in kind, a transfer of business, or any similar event in the relevant taxable year;
    (b) Where such enterprise takes over full-time youth employees, etc. or full-time employees from a related party provided for in Article 11 (1).
  (8)"Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act means an amount calculated by the following formula (excluding the aggregate of subsidies paid or to be paid by the State and public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions and reduced or exempted amounts for the equivalent to social insurance premium to be borne by the employer for social insurance falling under any subparagraph of Article 30-4 (4) of the Act for full-time youth employees, etc. for the relevant taxable year): <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 11, 2020>
  (Total salary and wages referred to in Article 20 (1) of the Income Tax Act, which are paid to full-time youth employees, etc. in the relevant taxable year ÷ Number of full-time youth employees, etc. in the relevant taxable year) × Social insurance premium rate
  (9)"Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (1) 2 of the Act means the amount calculated by the following formula (excluding the aggregate of subsidies paid or to be paid by the State and public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions and reduced or exempted amounts for the equivalent to social insurance premium to be borne by the employer for social insurance falling under any subparagraph of Article 30-4 (4) of the Act for full-time youth employees, etc. for the relevant taxable year): <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 11, 2020>
  (Total salary and wages referred to in Article 20 (1) of the Income Tax Act, which are paid to full-time employees, excluding youths, etc., in the relevant taxable year ÷ (Number of full-time employees in the relevant taxable year - Number of full-time youth employees, etc. in the relevant taxable year) × Social insurance premium rate
  (10) For purposes of paragraphs (8) and (9), the social insurance premium rate shall be the aggregate of the following applicable as of the end of the relevant taxable year: <Amended on Aug 31, 2012; Feb. 7, 2017>
  1. 1/2 of the insurance premium rate prescribed under Article 44 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the National Health Insurance Act;
  2. Number calculated by multiplying the number calculated under subparagraph 1 by the long-term care insurance premium rate prescribed under Article 4 of the Long-Term Care Insurance Act;
  3. The insurance premium rate prescribed under Article 88 of the National Pension Act;
  4. The aggregate of the numbers calculated under each subparagraph of Article 13 (4) of the Act on the Collection of Insurance Premiums for Employment Insurance and Industrial Accident Compensation Insurance;
  5. The industrial accident compensation insurance rate prescribed under Article 14 (3) of the Act on the Collection of Insurance Premiums for Employment Insurance and Industrial Accident Compensation Insurance.
  (11) The amount of income tax or corporate tax payable pursuant to the latter part of Article 30-4 (2) of the Act shall be calculated according to the following subparagraphs (limited to the amount of tax deducted pursuant to Article 30-4 (1) of the Act in the taxable year immediately preceding the relevant taxable year) and shall be paid as income tax or corporate tax when filing the tax return for the relevant taxable year: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Where the number of full-time employees decreased: An amount calculated as follows:
    (a) Where the reduced number of full-time youth employees is not less than the reduced number of full-time employees: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  A - B + C
  A: Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act mutatis mutandis to the number of persons calculated by subtracting the reduced number of full-time employees, as compared to the number in the year for which a deduction was granted (hereafter in this Article referred to as"first deduction year"), from the reduced number of full-time youth employees, etc. (limited to the increased number of the full-time youth employees in the first deduction year), as compared to the number in the first deduction year (hereafter in this formula referred to as"subtracted number of persons")
  B: Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 2 of the Act to the subtracted number of persons
  C: Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act to the reduced number of full-time employees, as compared to the number in the first deduction year
    (b) In other cases: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  A + B
  A: Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act mutatis mutandis to the reduced number of full-time youth employees (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees in the first deduction year), as compared to the number in the first deduction year
  B. Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act mutatis mutandis to the reduced number of full-time employees, except full-time youth employees, etc. (limited to the decreased number of full-time employees in the first deduction year), as compared to the number in the first deduction year
  2. Where the number of full-time employees has not decreased, but the number of full-time youth employees, etc. has decreased: An amount calculated according to the following formula:
  A + B
  A: Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act mutatis mutandis to the reduced number of full-time youth employees (limited to the increased number of full-time youth employees in the first deduction year; hereafter in this formula referred to as"reduced number of youth employees"), as compared to the number in the first deduction year
  B. Amount calculated by applying the formula prescribed in Article 30-4 (1) 1 of the Act mutatis mutandis to the reduced number of youth employees
  (12) For the purposes of paragraph (11), persons classified as full-time youth employees, etc. in the first deduction year shall be deemed full-time youth employees in subsequent taxable years thereafter for the purpose of calculating the number of full-time youth employees, etc. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (13)"Enterprise prescribed by Presidential Decree among small and medium enterprises" in Article 30-4 (3) of the Act means small and medium-sized enterprises that meet all of the following requirements: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. That the number of full-time employees of the enterprise shall be less than ten persons;
  2. That the tax base of income tax or corporate tax for the relevant taxable year shall not exceed five million won. In such cases, the tax base of income tax shall be limited to business income, and the calculation method shall be prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
  (14)"Employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (3) of the Act means employees whose hourly wage is between 100/100 and 120/100 of the minimum wage amount under Article 5 of the Minimum Wage Act among nationals who have entered into an employment contract under the Labor Standards Act. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (15)"Subsidies from the State, etc. prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (3) of the Act means the aggregate amount of the subsidies paid or to be paid by the State and public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions for the amount equivalent to the premiums of a social insurance which falls under any subparagraph of Article 30-4 (4) of the Act and is to be borne by the employer, and the amount of reductions or exemptions. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (16)"Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-4 (3) of the Act means the amount equivalent to the social insurance premiums to be borne by the employer less the amount referred to in paragraph (15). <Newly Inserted on Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 15, 2022>
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Feb. 2, 2012]
  [Title Amended on Feb. 13, 2018]

Article 27-5 (Special Taxation for Gift Tax on Start-Up Funds) (1)"Property prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as land and buildings" in the former part of Article 30-5 (1) of the Act means any property specified in Article 94 (1) of the Income Tax Act. <Amended on Feb. 22, 2008; Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 21, 2014>
  (2)"Business start-up fund prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30-5 (1) of the Act means either of the following funds used directly for starting a business specified in Article 30-5 (2) of the Act: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 5, 2016; Aug. 28, 2018; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. Funds for acquiring business assets prescribed in Article 5 (19);
  2. Payments made for security deposits and rents for the place of business (including security money for lease on a deposit basis; hereinafter the same shall apply).
  (3)"Commence his/her business" or"business startup" in the former part and the latter part of Article 30-5 (2) of the Act, with the exception of its subparagraphs, means registration of a business with the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment under Article 168 (1) of the Income Tax Act, Article 111 (1) of the Corporate Tax Act, or Article 8 (1) or (5) of the Value-Added Tax Act; and"situations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 30-5 (2) of the Act, with the exception of its subparagraphs, means where a person acquires a business asset under Article 5 (19) or pays a security deposit or a rent for an extended place of business. <Amended on Jun. 28, 2013; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (4)"Business assets prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-5 (2) 1-2 of the Act means the business assets prescribed in Article 5 (19). <Newly Inserted on Feb. 28, 2023>
  (5)"Ratio prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-5 (2) 1-2 of the Act means 30/100. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 28, 2023>
  (6)"Date prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30-5 (5) of the Act means: <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. The end of the month following the month in which the date of start-up falls;
  2. The deadline for filing the tax return each taxable year by the four subsequent taxable years (where the start-up funds are fully used, the taxable year in which the date such start-up funds are used falls) from the taxable year in which the date of start-up falls.
  (7)"Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-5 (2) 4 of the Act means where start-up funds are used for operating the business in which a person has engaged before receiving donated start-up funds or for replacing plant and equipment for such business. <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (8) The following information shall be stated in a statement on the spending of start-up funds submitted under the former part of Article 30-5 (5) of the Act: <Amended on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. Details of the donated start-up funds;
  2. Details of the use of the donated start-up funds and materials evidencing such details;
  3. Materials evidencing details of employment, if the donated start-up funds exceed five billion won.
  (9) The equivalent to the interest, which is added to gift tax levied under the latter part of Article 30-5 (6) of the Act shall be calculated by multiplying the amount of subparagraph 1 by the period of subparagraph 2 and the rate of subparagraph 3: <Amended on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. The amount of gift tax determined pursuant to the former part of Article 30-5 (6) of the Act, with the exception of its subparagraphs;
  2. The period from the day following a deadline for filing the tax return of gift tax on the first-donated start-up funds until the date the grounds for additional collection arise;
  3. The rate specified in Article 11-2 (9) 2.
  (10)"Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-5 (6) 6 of the Act means any of the following: <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. Where a donee dies: Provided, That the same shall not apply to the following cases:
    (a) Where a donee dies after receiving donated start-up funds, but before commencing his/her business pursuant to Article 30-5 (2) of the Act; and the heir of the donee commences the business pursuant to Article 30-5 (2) through (6) of the same Act after succeeding to the donee's status;
    (b) Where a donee dies after receiving donated start-up funds and commencing his/her business pursuant to Article 30-5 (2) of the Act, but before using the start-up funds for the start-up objectives provided for in Article 30-5 (4) of the Act; and the heir of the donee commences the business pursuant to Article 30-5 (4) through (6) of the same Act after succeeding to the donee's status;
    (c) Where a donee dies after receiving donated start-up funds and completing the commencement of his/her business pursuant to Article 30-5 (4) of the Act; and the heir of the donee commences the business pursuant to Article 30-5 (6) of the same Act after succeeding to the donee's status;
  2. Where a donee discontinues or suspends his/her business (including actual suspension of the business): Provided, That the same shall not apply where the donee discontinues or suspends his/her business on either of the following grounds:
    (a) Where the donee discontinues his/her business on the grounds that his/her debt exceeds his/her asset;
    (b) Where the donee suspends or discontinues his/her business (limited to either one of suspension or discontinuation of the business) for the period not exceeding two years (where he/she discontinues his/her business, referring to two years by the time he/she resumes his/her business after discontinuing his/her business) only once on the grounds of his/her business need or his/her business conversion after first commencing his/her business.
  (11)"Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-5 (6) 6 of the Act means start-up funds (including the portion of the value increased on the grounds of the start-up). <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (12) For the purposes of Article 30-5 (6) 7 of the Act,"employees" means full-time employees prescribed in Article 27-3 (4). In such cases, the number of workers shall be calculated by dividing the aggregate of the number of employees as at the end of each month in the relevant taxable year by the number of months in the relevant taxable year. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (13) A person who files a tax return on gift tax and interest thereon pursuant to Article 30-5 (7) of the Act shall submit a statement on the reason for violation of special taxation on gift tax for start-up funds and a calculation sheet for voluntary payment, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 28, 2023>
  (14) Pursuant to Article 30-5 (12) of the Act, a person who wishes to be eligible for the special taxation under paragraph (1) of that Article shall submit an application for special taxation for start-up funds and a statement on the use of start-up funds, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of a tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment at the time of filing a tax return on gift tax. <Amended on Feb. 28, 2023>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 9, 2006]

Article 27-6 (Special Taxation for Gift Tax on Succession to Family Business) (1) "Where a resident succeeds to a family business, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-6 (1) of the Act means where a person to whom stocks or equity shares of a family business (hereafter in this Article, referred to as "stocks, etc.") are conveyed as a gift (hereafter in this Article and Articles 28 and 29, referred to as "donee") or his/her spouse, engages in the family business until the deadline for filing a tax return on gift tax under Article 68 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act, and takes office as representative director within five years from the date of conveyance as a gift. <Amended on Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  (2)"Amount calculated by the method prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 30-6 of the Act means an amount calculated as follows: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 11, 2020>
  1. Where two or more residents receive stocks, etc. as a gift on the same day: An amount calculated by allocating the amount of gift tax imposed under Article 30-6 of the Act to each resident in proportion to the value of the stocks, etc. received by each resident as a gift, deeming that one of the residents receive all of the stocks, etc. as a gift;
  2. Where another resident received stocks, etc. in the relevant family business before the date of conveyance of the relevant stocks, etc. as a gift and became liable for gift tax imposed under Article 30-6 of the Act: The amount of gift tax imposed under Article 30-6 of the act, deeming that the other resident is the donee of the relevant stocks, etc.
  (3)"Where a person fails to succeed to the family business" in Article 30-6 (3) of the Act means where the donee fails to succeed to the family business as provided for in paragraph (1). <Amended on Feb. 11. 2020>
  (4)"Just grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30-6 (3) of the Act, with the exception of its subparagraphs, means any of the following circumstances: <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Oct. 7, 2008; Feb. 11. 2020>
  1. Where a donee has died and the heir of the donee engages in the family business after succeeding to the initial status of the donee by the filing deadline for filing a tax return under Article 67 of the Inheritance and Gift Tax Act;
  2. Where a donee donates the stocks, etc. conveyed as a gift, to the State or a local government;
  3. Where other extenuating circumstances prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance arise.
  (5) The equivalent to the interest, which is added to gift tax levied under the latter part of Article 30-6 (3) of the Act, with the exception of its subparagraphs, shall be calculated by multiplying the amount of subparagraph 1 by the period of subparagraph 2 and the rate of subparagraph 3: <Amended on Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. The amount of gift tax determined pursuant to the former part of Article 30-6 (3) of the Act, with the exception of its subparagraphs;
  2. The period from the day following a deadline for filing the tax return of gift tax on the first-donated stocks, etc., until the date the grounds for additional collection arise;
  3. The rate specified in Article 11-2 (9) 2.
  (6) Circumstances provided for in Article 30-6 (3) 1 of the Act shall include the following: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Where the done (including the spouse of the done referred to in paragraph (1)) fails to continue to hold office as representative director for five years from the date of conveyance of stocks, etc. as a gift;
  2. Where it falls under Article 15 (11) 2 or 3 of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act;
  3. Deleted; <Feb. 29, 2024>
  (7) Circumstances provided for in Article 30-6 (3) 2 of the Act shall include the following: <Amended on Feb. 2, 2012; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 11, 2020>
  1. Where the done disposes of the stocks, etc. conveyed as a gift: Provided, That the following cases shall be excluded here from:
    (a) Where the done becomes the largest stockholder, etc. defined under Article 15 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"largest stockholder, etc.") as a consequence of restructuring, such as a merger or split-off;
    (b) Where the done reduces his/her shares in order to meet the requirements for listing specified in the Listing Regulations pursuant to Article 390 (1) of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act;
  2. Where the dome's holding ratio decreases due to forfeiture of his/her rights, etc. in the course of increasing the paid-in capital of the corporation that issued the stocks, etc. conveyed as a gift: Provided, That any of the following cases shall be excluded here from:
    (a) Where the relevant corporation increases its paid-in capital by issuing new stocks in order to increase its investment in plant and equipment or to expand its business, and the done is forfeited his/her rights in order to allocate new stocks to any person, other than the related persons (referring to the persons defined under Article 2-2 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act; hereafter in this Article, the same shall apply) to the done, but the done falls under the largest stockholder, etc.;
    (b) Where the dome's holding ratio decreases due to a debt-for-equity swap of the relevant corporation, but the done becomes the largest stockholder, etc.
  3. Where the done ceases to be the largest stockholder, etc. because his/her holding ratio decreases due to the disposal of stocks or forfeiture, etc. in the course of increasing the paid-in capital by any related person to the done.
  (8) A taxpayer may be granted special taxation for gift tax under Article 30-6 (1) of the Act on the aggregate of the taxable value of the stocks, etc. eligible for special taxation of gift tax and the gains from donation, subject to a ceiling of ten billion won, with regard to gains from donation under Article 41-3 or 41-5 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act (hereafter in this paragraph, referred to as"gains from donation"), which accrue from the donation of stocks after the taxpayer receives stocks, etc. eligible for special taxation of gift tax under Article 30-6 (1) of the Act. In such cases, gains from donation granted special taxation shall be added to the taxable value of inheritance tax under Articles 30-5 (7) and (8) and 30-6 (4) of the Act, notwithstanding Article 13 (3) of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act. <Amended on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 11, 2020>
  (9) Where an inheritance commences after stocks, etc. eligible for special taxation of gift tax under Article 30-6 (1) of the Act were conveyed as a gift; and each of the following requirements are satisfied as at the commencement date of inheritance, relevant provisions shall apply by deeming such case inheritance of a family business under Article 18-2 (1) of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act: <Amended on Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. It shall be the family business prescribed in the former part of the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 18-2 (1) of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act (the average amount of turnover, among the relevant requirements, shall be determined on the basis of the average amount of turnover for three business years immediately preceding the business year in which stocks, etc. are conveyed as a gift pursuant to Article 30-6 (1) of the Act; but if the requirement of Article 15 (3) 1 (a) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act is not met, it shall be deemed that the decedent holds the stocks, etc. conveyed to the heir as a gift until the commencement date of inheritance in applying the requirement of that item): Provided, That Article 15 (3) 1 (b) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act shall not apply;
  2. Deleted. <Jun. 3, 2011>
  3. The done engages in the family business or holds office as representative director where he/she has not disposed of the stocks, etc. conveyed as a gift or his/her holding ratio has not decreased.
  (10) "Equivalent to the property of family business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-6 (1) of the Act means an amount calculated by applying mutatis mutandisArticle 15 (5) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act. In such cases, "commencement date of inheritance" shall be construed as "date of conveyance as a gift". <Newly Inserted on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 11, 2020; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  (11) "Fine prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-6 (4) of the Act means any of the fines prescribed in the subparagraphs of Article 15 (19) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 29, 2024>
  (12) "Amount corresponding to interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the latter part of Article 30-6 (4) 2 of the Act means an amount calculated by multiplying the amount specified in subparagraph 1 by the period specified in subparagraph 2 and the ratio specified in subparagraph 3: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. The amount of gift tax determined pursuant to the former part of Article 30-6 (4) 2 of the Act;
  2. The period from the day after the deadline for filing a tax return on gift tax on stocks, etc. originally received as a gift to the day on which any of the events referred to in Article 30-6 (4) 2 of the Act occurs;
  3. The rate pursuant to Article 27-4 of the Enforcement Decree of the National Tax Act.
  (13) When filing a tax return on gift tax and interest thereon pursuant to Article 30-6 (8) of the Act, a statement on the reason for additional collection of gift tax on succession to the family business eligible for special taxation and a statement of voluntary payment shall be submitted in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 13, 2018; Feb. 11. 2020; Feb. 29, 2024>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 27-7 (Deferral of Payment of Gift Tax for Succession to Family Business) (1) A resident who intends to apply for payment deferral pursuant to Article 30-7 (1) or (6) of the Act shall submit the following documents to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment at the time of filing a tax return on inheritance tax or gift tax under Article 67 or 68 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act (including a revised return under Article 45 of the Framework Act on National Taxes or a tax return after due date under Article 45-3 of that Act): Provided, That a person who has received a notice of determination of the tax base and tax amount pursuant to Article 77 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act may submit such documents by the due date for payment designated in the notice.
  1. An application for payment deferral in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance;
  2. Documents proving that the special taxation under Article 30-6 the Act or the permission for payment deferral under Article 30-7 of the Act has been granted (applicable only to applications filed pursuant to Article 30-7 (6) 1 of the Act);
  3. Documents proving that a deduction for inheritance of a family business under Article 18-2 (1) of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act or the permission for payment deferral under Article 72-2 (1) of that Act (applicable only for applications filed under Article 30-7 (6) 2 of the Act).
  (2) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (1), the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment shall notify the applicant in writing of the grant or denial of the permission within a period prescribed as follows:
  1. In cases of a tax return on inheritance tax filed pursuant to Article 67 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act: Nine months from the day after the deadline for filing the tax return under paragraph (1) of that Article;
  2. In cases of a tax return on gift tax filed pursuant to Article 68 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act: Six months from the day after the deadline for filing the tax return under paragraph (1) of that Article;
  3. In cases of a revised return filed pursuant to Article 45 of the Framework Act on National Taxes or a tax return filed after due date pursuant to Article 45-3 of that Act: Six months from the end of the month in which the revised return or return after due date is filed (or nine months in cases of an application filed pursuant to Article 30-7 (6) 2 of the Act);
  4. In cases of the provision of paragraph (1), with the exception of its subparagraphs: 14 days after the due date for payment according to the payment notice.
  (3) If a notice under paragraph (2) 4 is given after the due date for payment according to the payment notice, no additional tax for delayed payment shall be imposed under Article 47-4 (1) 1 (limited to the portion accruing from the day after the due date for payment according to the payment notice) or 3 of the Framework Act on National Taxes for the period prior to the date of the notice.
  (4)"Amount prescribed in Presidential Decree" In the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-7 (1) of the Act means an amount calculated according to the following formula. In such cases, the equivalent to the value of family business assets in the formula means an amount calculated according to Article 15 (5) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act, and"date of inheritance" in that subparagraph shall be construed as"date of conveyance as a gift":
  Amount payable as gift tax × Equivalent to value of family business assets/Total value of assets conveyed as a gift
  (5) In order to be granted permission to defer payment of gift tax pursuant to Article 30-7 (1) of the Act, a resident or his/her spouse who received stocks or equity shares in a family business (hereafter in this Article referred to as"stocks, etc.") pursuant to subparagraph 1 of that paragraph shall be engaged in the family business by not later than the deadline for filing a tax return on gift tax pursuant to Article 68 of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act and shall take office as representative director within three years from the date of conveyance as a gift.
  (6)"Small and medium enterprises prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-7 (1) 1 of the Act means small and medium enterprises under Article 15 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act.
  (7)"Good cause prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-7 (3) of the Act means a case falling under any subparagraph of Article 27-6 (4) (except subparagraph 1 of that paragraph).
  (8) For the purposes of Article 30-7 (3) 1 of the Act, a resident shall be deemed to have ceased to be engaged in a family business in any of the following cases:
  1. Where the resident (including the resident's spouse under paragraph (5)) who received stocks, etc. of a family business as a gift does not hold office as representative director (within five years from the date of conveyance as a gift);
  2. Where the family business is suspended (or has no business performance) for not less than one year or is closed.
  (9)"Where the equity shares of the resident…decrease" in the provisions, without the exception of the subparagraphs" of Article 30-7 (3) 2 of the Act includes cases falling under any subparagraph of Article 27-6 (7).
  (10)"Tax amount calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree in consideration of the ratio of the decrease in the equity shares" in Article 30-7 (3) 2 (b) and the latter part of Article 30-7 (7) of the Act means an amount calculated according to the following formula:
  Tax amount = A × (B + C)
  A: Tax amount for which payment is deferred under Article 30-7 (1) of the Act
  B: Decreased ratio of equity shares
  C: Ratio of equity shares as at the date of conveyance as a gift
  (11)"Regular employees prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-7 (3) 3 (a) of the Act means employees who hold a contract concluded under the Labor Standards Act: Provided, That persons falling under any subparagraph of Article 15 (13) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act are excluded herefrom.
  (12)"Gross salary amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30-7 (3) 3 (b) of the Act means the total amount of income under Article 20 (1) 1 and 2 of the Income Tax Act, paid to an employee pursuant to the main clause of paragraph 11 (excluding persons falling under Article 26 -4 (2) 3, but including those persons if the persons falling under that paragraph are only persons who exist).
  (13) Articles 15 (17) and (18) of the Enforcement Decree of the Inheritance Tax and Gift Tax Act shall apply to the calculation of the number of regular employees and the gross salary amount under Article 30-7 (3) 3 (a) and (b) of the Act.
  (14)"Interest calculated thereon as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exceptions of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-7 (3) of the Act means an amount calculated by multiplying the amount in subparagraph 1 by the period in subparagraph 2 and the rate in subparagraph 3 (or, in cases where permission was granted for payment deferral under Article 30-7 (6) of the Act, 50/100 of the rate in subparagraph 3):
  1. The amount of gift tax determined pursuant to the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-7 (3) of the Act;
  2. The period from the day after the deadline for filing a tax return on gift tax on stocks, etc. in a family business originally received as a gift to the day on which any of the events referred to in Article 30-7 (3) of the Act occurs;
  3. The interest rate calculated by diving the interest rate in the main clause of Article 43-3 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes at the time of the revocation or change of permission for payment deferral under Article 30-7 (3) of the Act by 365: Provided, That if the interest rate in the main clause of Article 43-3 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes is changed once or more during the period of subparagraph 2, the interest rate calculated by dividing the rate before the change by 365 shall be applied to the period before the change.
  (15)"Interest calculated thereon as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exceptions of the subparagraphs, of Article 30-7 (5) of the Act means an amount calculated by multiplying the amount in subparagraph 1 by the period in subparagraph 2 and the rate in subparagraph 3 (or, in cases where permission was granted for payment deferral under Article 30-7 (6) of the Act, 50/100 of the rate in subparagraph 3):
  1. The amount of gift tax under Article 30-7 (5) of the Act;
  2. The period from the day after the deadline for filing a tax return on gift tax on stocks, etc. in a family business originally received as a gift to the day on which any of the events referred to in Article 30-7 (5) of the Act occurs;
  3. The interest rate calculated by diving the interest rate in the main clause of Article 43-3 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes at the time of the revocation or change of permission for payment deferral under Article 30-7 (5) of the Act by 365: Provided, That if the interest rate in the main clause of Article 43-3 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on National Taxes is changed once or more during the period of subparagraph 2, the interest rate calculated by dividing the rate before the change by 365 shall be applied to the period before the change.
  (16) A person who files a tax return on gift tax and interest thereon pursuant to Article 30-7 (4) of the Act shall submit a statement on the reason for additional collection for ex-post management of payment deferral and a statement of voluntary payment, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.
  (17) The head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment shall check whether a resident who has been granted permission for payment deferral falls under any subparagraph of Article 30-7 of the Act for the purpose of management.
