  5. Any other amount prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance as the amount disbursed for mutually-beneficial cooperation.
  (15)"Period prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 100-32 (3) of the Act means either of the following periods:
  1. Where a domestic corporation files a return by choosing the method provided for in Article 100-32 (2) 1 of the Act: The business year in which three years elapse;
  2. Where a domestic corporation files a return by choosing the method provided for in Article 100-32 (2) 2 of the Act: The business year in which one year elapses;
  (16) Where a corporation subject to continuous application of the method chosen under Article 100-32 (3) of the Act merges with another corporation or acquires the business of another corporation, or in circumstances prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, it may change the method chosen.
  (17) Where a domestic corporation has not chosen any of the methods provided for in subparagraphs of Article 100-32 (2) of the Act, the domestic corporation shall be deemed to have chosen a method by which the smaller amount of unappropriated earnings or the greater over-appropriated amount is computed for the business year that falls under any subparagraph of Article 100-32 (1) of the Act for the first time in filing the relevant tax return.
  (18) Even where a domestic corporation that sets aside the reserve for appropriation for the next term during the relevant business year and deducts the reserve from unappropriated earnings pursuant to Article 100-32 (5) of the Act ceases to be a domestic corporation that belongs to a corporate group subject to limitations on cross shareholding under Article 31 (1) of the Monopoly Regulation and Fair Trade Act during the following two business years, it shall pay corporate tax on unappropriated earnings in accordance with Article 100-32 (1) and (6) of that Act. <Amended on Feb. 28, 2023>
  (19) For the purposes of Article 100-32 (7) of the Act, if an over-appropriated amount is deducted, pursuant to Article 56 (6) of the Corporate Tax Act, from the reserve for appropriation in the next term accumulated in the immediately preceding business year pursuant to Article 56 (5) of the Corporate Tax Act (referring to that Act before it is amended by Act No. 16008), the amount left over after deducting the amount of subparagraph 2 from the amount of subparagraph 1 may be carried over to the next business year and deducted from the unappropriated income of the next year: <Amended on Feb. 12, 2019>
  1. The over-appropriated amount of the relevant business year, calculated pursuant to Article 100-32 (2) of the Act;
  2. The over-appropriated amount deducted from the reserve for appropriation in the next term pursuant to Article 56 (6) of the Corporate Tax Act (referring to that Act before it is amended by Act No. 16008).
  (20)"Where a domestic corporation referred to in paragraph (1) has disposed of an asset referred to in paragraph (2) 1 (a), or in circumstances prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 100-32 (8) of the Act means the following cases: <Amended on Feb. 12, 2019; Jan. 5, 2021; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. Where the relevant asset is transferred or lent before two years pass from the completion date of investment in the asset under paragraph (6) 1 (a) (i) or the purchase date of the asset (limited to purchased assets) under paragraph (6) 1 (b), or the acquisition date of the asset under paragraph (6) 2: Provided, That this shall not apply where the asset falls under any of the following items:
