  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 104-12 (Method of Calculating Tax Amount of Special Provisions on Taxation of Gross Real Estate Tax on Confucian Schools and Religious Organizations) (1) Where an individual organization reports the gross real estate tax for house under Article 104-13 (1) of the Act, the"total amount of tax amount imposed as property tax for house" in the arithmetic formula in Article 4-2 of the Enforcement Decree of theGross Real Estate Tax Act shall include the property tax for house which should have been imposed deeming that the individual organization possesses the house in question.
  (2) Where an individual organization reports the gross real estate tax for land under Article 104-13 (1) of the Act, the"total amount of tax amount imposed as property tax for land, which is the object of composite cumulative taxation" in the arithmetic formula in Article 5-3 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of theGross Real Estate Tax Act or the"total amount of tax amount imposed as property tax for land, which is the object of separate cumulative taxation" in the arithmetic formula in Article 5-3 (2) of the same Decree shall include the property tax for land which should have been imposed deeming that the individual organization possesses the land in question.
  (3) Where the Confucian school foundation, etc. report the gross real estate tax for house deeming that they do not possess the house in question under Article 104-13 (3) of the Act, the"total amount of tax amount imposed as property tax for house" in the arithmetic formula in Article 4-2 of the Enforcement Decree of theGross Real Estate Tax Act shall be the property tax for house which should have been imposed deeming that the Confucian school foundation, etc. do not possess the house in question.
  (4) Where the Confucian school, etc. report the gross real estate tax for land deeming that they do not possess the land in question under Article 104-13 (3) of the Act, the"total amount of tax amount imposed as property tax for land, which is the object of composite cumulative taxation" in the arithmetic formula in Article 5-3 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of theGross Real Estate Tax Act or the"total amount of tax amount imposed as property tax for land, which is the object of separate cumulative taxation" in the arithmetic formula in Article 5-3 (2) of the same Decree shall be the property tax for land which should have been imposed deeming that the Confucian school foundation, etc. do not possess the land in question.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 104-13 (Report on Special Cases of Taxation of Gross Real Estate Tax for Confucian Schools and Religious Organizations) (1) The individual organization and Confucian school foundation, etc. that intend to report under Article 104-13 (1) and (3) of the Act shall submit a report of special taxation of gross real estate tax of Confucian school and religious organization prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, written permission for modification of articles of incorporation of Confucian school foundation from the competent authority under Article 45 (3) of the Civil Act, articles of incorporation and meeting minutes of the board of directors of Confucian school foundation, etc., other papers proving that the house in question or the land in question is actually possessed by the individual organization in addition to the papers under subparagraphs of Article 8 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of theGross Real Estate Tax Act between September 16 through September 30 of the year concerned to the head of tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Feb. 4, 2009>
  (2) Where there is no change in the proprietary relations of the house in question or land in question from the year next to the year when report under Article 104-13 (1) and (3) of the Act was made for the first time, the papers proving that the house in question or the land in question is actually possessed by the individual organization except for the report of special taxation of gross real estate tax of Confucian school and religious organization under paragraph (1) may not be submitted.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 104-14 (Application for Tax Credit for Third Party Logistics Expenses) (1) Deleted. <Feb. 17, 2021>
  (2) A person who wishes to be granted a deduction of income tax or corporate tax under Article 104-14 (1) and (2) of the Act shall submit an application for tax deduction in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with his/her tax return. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Feb. 12, 2019>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 104-15 (Special Taxation for Investment in Development of Overseas Resources) (1) "Contributions prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-15 (1) 2 of the Act means contribution to a foreign corporation meeting all the following requirements which occupies at least 10/100 of the total number of issued stocks or total amount of contribution, or contribution in cases where the executive officers or employees of an overseas resources development business operator under subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Overseas Resources Development Business Act (hereinafter referred to as "overseas resources development business operator") is dispatched as the executive officers or employees of a foreign corporation: <Amended on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. That the overseas resources development business operator shall have a mining right or mining right by lease to the mining area (hereafter referred to as "relevant mining area" in this Article) of the business reported under Article 5 of that Act;
  2. That it shall have been established for the purpose of development and operation of the relevant mining area.
  (2)"Investment prescribed by Presidential Decree pursuant to Article 3 (1) 18 (a) of the Foreign Exchange Transactions Act" in Article 104-15 (1) 3 of the Act means any of the following investment: <Amended on Jun. 3, 2011>
  1. Investment for participating in the capital increase of a foreign subsidiary (referring to a foreign corporation in which a Korean resident directly invests 100/100 of the total number of issued stocks or the total amount of investment; hereinafter the same shall apply in this Article) owned by a person with Korean nationality;
  2. Investment for lending money to a foreign subsidiary owned by a national with a redemption period of at least five years;
  3. Investment made by an overseas resources development project operator jointly with a national under subparagraph 1 or 2 to lend money to a foreign subsidiary owned by a Korean resident with a redemption period of at least five years.
  (3) The investment or contribution for the development of mineral resources of an overseas resources developer when Article 104-15 (1) of the Act is applied shall be limited to the amount of mining right or concession acquired or being held as prescribed in subparagraphs of Article 104-15 (1) of the Act, which shall be calculated by multiplying the total investment (limited to the amount of mining right or concession) by the investment ratio of each overseas resources developer in cases under paragraph (2) 3. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 4, 2009>
  (4) "Amounts prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-15 (2) of the Act means the amounts classified as follows: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Where it falls under Article 104-15 (2) 1 of the Act: Amount calculated according to the following formula;
  Tax amount deducted pursuant to Article 104-15 (1) of the Act x (Acquisition value of transferred or recovered investment assets or investment shares/Total acquisition value of investment assets or investment shares)
  2. Where it falls under Article 104-15 (2) 2 of the Act: The full amount of tax deducted pursuant to Article 104-15 (1) of the Act.
  (5) The additional amount equivalent to interest under Article 104-15 (2) of the Act shall be the amount calculated by multiplying the deducted tax amount by the period under subparagraph 1 and the rate under subparagraph 2. <Amended on Feb. 4, 2009; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Period from the day next to the day of a report of a tax base in the taxable year in which deduction was granted until the day of a report of a tax base of the taxable year in which the reason in Article 104-15 (2) of the Act occurred;
  2. The rate specified in Article 11-2 (9) 2.
  (6) Those who intend to be subject to Article 104-15 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for tax deduction and a report of investment in the overseas resources development prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance along with a tax base return to the head of a tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Feb. 4, 2009; Feb. 29, 2024>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 104-16 (Special Taxation for Financial Soundness of Universities and Colleges) (1)"Primary assets for profit-making prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 104-16 (1) of the Act means land and buildings among the basic assets for profit-making under Article 7 of the Regulations on the Establishment and Operation of Universities and Colleges.
  (2)"Acquiring another primary assets for profit-making within one year from the date of transfer" in the former part of Article 104-16 (1) of the Act, includes acquiring another basic assets for profit-making after the end of the business year in which the previous basic assets for profit-making are disposed of.
  (3)"Amount calculated by the formula prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 104-16 (1) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the amount in subparagraph 1 by the rate in subparagraph 2: <Amended on Feb. 12, 2019>
  1. The disposal price of endowment for profit-making being disposed of - (book value of the endowment for profit-making being disposed of + deficit carried-forward under Article 13 (1) 1 of the Corporate Tax Act as at the end of immediately previous business year);
  2. The ratio of acquisition value of endowment for profit-making being acquired to the disposal price of endowment for profit-making being disposed of (the ratio shall not exceed 100/100).
  (4) For the purposes of paragraph (3), where another endowment for profit-making has not been acquired by the end of business year in which the previous endowment for profit-making are transferred, the price of asset scheduled for acquisition (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"value of asset scheduled for acquisition") may be the price of endowment for profit-making being acquired.
  (5)"Amount calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 104-16 (2) of the Act means the whole of the amount (referring to the amount exceeding the amount calculated under paragraph (3) on the basis of actual acquisition value where an asset with a value less than the value of asset scheduled for acquisition has been acquired) that has not been included in the profit under paragraph (3).
  (6) An educational foundation that intends to be eligible under Article 104-16 (1) of the Act shall submit the details of transfer gains and statement of split profit, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with a tax return of the business year in which the endowment for profit-making are transferred. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008>
  (7) When endowment for profit-making is acquired after having paragraph (4) applied, a report of completion of acquisition in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, along with a tax return of the business year in which such assets are acquired, shall be submitted to the head of tax office having jurisdiction over place of tax payment. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 22, 2008]

Article 104-17 Deleted. <Feb. 17, 2021>

Article 104-18 (Special Provisions concerning Taxation for Land Acquired by Housing Construction Business Operator) (1) Those who intend to have Article 104-19 of the Act applied to themselves shall file a return prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance: Provided, That there are no changes in the filed matters from the year next to the year in which a return was filed for the first time, he/she may not file a return.
  (2) The amount of gross real estate tax in Article 104-19 (3) of the Act means the amount obtained by subtracting the amount in subparagraph 2 from the amount in subparagraph 1:
  1. Tax amount calculated by deeming the land concerned that has not been included in the object liable for summing up of tax base as prescribed in Article 104-19 (1) of the Act as the land included in the object liable for summing up of tax base of gross real estate tax in each taxable year;
  2. Tax amount calculated by deeming the land concerned that has not been included in the object liable for summing up of tax base as prescribed in Article 104-19 (1) of the Act as the land excluded from the object liable for summing up of tax base of gross real estate tax in each taxable year.
  (3) The additional amount equivalent to interest in Article 104-19 (3) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the amount of gross real estate tax under paragraph (2) by the period under subparagraph 1 and by the rate under subparagraph 2: <Amended on Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Period from the day next to the deadline for payment in each taxable year that has been reported under Article 104-19 (2) of the Act until the day when the tax amount to be collected additionally as prescribed in Article 104-19 (3) of the Act is notified;
  2. The rate specified in Article 11-2 (9) 2.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 4, 2009]

Article 104-19 (Special Taxation for Corporate Tax on Consolidation of Korea National Housing Corporation and Korea Land Corporation) (1) The amount to be included in deductible expense as prescribed in Article 104-21 (1) of the Act shall be an amount deemed profit dividends or surpluses distributed, calculated as prescribed in Article 16 (1) 5 of the Corporate Tax Act. In such cases, such amount shall be recognized as the advanced depreciation provision of the relevant stocks or equity shares (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"stocks, etc.").
  (2) The advanced depreciation provision recognized as prescribed in paragraph (1), shall be included in the gross income in the business year in which the stockholders, etc. of the Korea National Housing Corporation or the Korea Land Corporation dispose of the stocks of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation acquired in compensation for the merger, however, where some of such stocks, etc. are disposed of, an amount calculated by the following formula shall be included in the gross income:
  Advanced depreciation provision × (Number of stocks, etc. disposed of among the stocks, etc. of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation acquired in compensation for the merger ÷ Number of stocks, etc. of the Korea Land and Housing Corporation acquired in compensation for the merger)
  (3) Deleted. <Dec. 30, 2014>
  (4) A domestic corporation that intends to be eligible under Article 104-21 (1) of the Act shall submit a statement of adjustment of inclusion in deductible expense of an amount equivalent to deemed dividends, etc., in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, when it files a tax return under Article 60 of the Corporate Tax Act.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 18, 2010]

Article 104-20 (Special Taxation for Establishment and Operation of Corporate Sport Teams) (1)"Sport team for any event prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-22 (1) of the Act means a sport team for an event prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, among events of sport organizations affiliated with the Korean Sport and Olympic Committee established pursuant to Article 33 of the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as"Korean Sport and Olympic Committee"), which meets each of the following requirements that: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. The sport team shall be established (or re-established) and operated with players registered with a sport organization affiliated with the Korean Sport and Olympic Committee or the Korea Paralympic Committee established pursuant to Article 34 of the National Sports Promotion Act (hereinafter referred to as"Korea Paralympic Committee");
  2. The number of players per sport event shall be not less than the prescribed number of the relevant event;
  3. The sport team shall have at least one sport instructor for each sport event.
  (2)"Sport team for persons with disabilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-22 (2) of the Act means a sport team for an event for which a sport organization affiliated with the Korea Sports Association for the Disabled exists, which satisfies each of the requirements prescribed under paragraph (1). <Newly Inserted on Feb. 21, 2014>
  (3)"Team for the games prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-22 (2) of the Act means an e-sports team for the games prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, among the games selected pursuant to Article 12 of the Act on Promotion of E-Sports (Electronic Sports), which meets all the following requirements: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. The sport team shall be established (or re-established) and operated with e-sports players defined in the Act on Promotion of E-Sports (Electronic Sports);
  2. The sport team shall have at least one sport instructor for each sports game.
  (4)"Expenses prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-22 (1) through (3) of the Act means: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Personnel expenses for players, directors, and coaches of a sport team or an e-sports team under paragraphs (1) through (3) (hereafter in this paragraph referred to as"sport team") and persons who directly support operations of the sport team;
  2. Expenses prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance as those incurred in operating a sport team, such as expenses incurred in participating in competitions and purchasing training equipment.
  (5) A domestic corporation that seeks a tax credit under Article 104-22 (1) through (3) of the Act shall file an application for the tax credit in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance with the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with a tax return. <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (6)"Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree concerning the composition, etc. of sport teams" in Article 104-22 (5) of the Act means the requirements prescribed in paragraph (1) or (3). <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 15, 2022>
  (7)"Equivalent to the interest calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-22 (4) of the Act means an amount calculated by multiplying the amount of tax deducted under Article 104-22 (1) or (2) of the Act, by the period under subparagraph 1 and the rate under subparagraph 2: <Amended on Feb. 21, 2014; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 15, 2022>
  1. Period from the day following the end of the taxable year in which deduction is granted, until the end of the taxable year in which a ground for payment arises;
  2. The rate specified in Article 11-2 (9) 2.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Dec. 30, 2010]

Article 104-21 (Tax Reductions or Exemptions for Overseas Korean Enterprises on their Return to Korea) (1)"Person prescribed by Presidential Decree, including a Korean national" in Article 104-24 (1) of the Act means a Korean national (including an overseas Korean entitled to stay as overseas Korean under Article 5 of the Act on the Immigration and Legal Status of Overseas Koreans) or a corporation incorporated under the law of the Republic of Korea (including a foreign-capital-invested company defined in subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Foreign Investment Promotion Act) who owns an overseas place of business operated continuously by him/her for at least two years, or takes de facto control over it, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance; and a person who relocates his/her place of business to the Republic of Korea pursuant to Article 104-24 (1) 1 of the Act shall meet one of the following requirements that: <Amended on Aug. 15, 2013; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 14, 2020; Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1. The person shall transfer or close his/her overseas place of business within four years from the date he/she commences a business by incorporating a business or establishing or expanding a place of business in an area outside the over-concentration control region of the Seoul Metropolitan area;
  2. The person shall incorporate a business or establish or expand a place of business in an area outside the over-concentration control region of the Seoul Metropolitan area within three years from the date he/she has transferred or closed his/her overseas place of business.
  (2) Deleted. <Feb. 29, 2024>
  (3) A person who returns to the Republic of Korea pursuant to Article 104-24 (1) 2 of the Act shall meet any of the following requirements that: <Newly Inserted on Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 15, 2022; Feb. 28, 2023>
  1 The person is a national who has no place of business in the Republic of Korea and establishes a new business in an area outside of the over-concentration control region of the Seoul Metropolitan area;
  2. The person who downsized an overseas place of business operated by him/her and had the downsizing confirmed by the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy pursuant to public notification issued by the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy under Article 6 (2) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Assistance to Korean Off-Shore Enterprises in Repatriation establishes or expands a place of business in an area outside of the over-concentration control region of the Seoul Metropolitan area within three years from the beginning of the taxable year following the taxable year in which the downsizing was completed.
  (4)"Overseas place of business" in Article 104-24 (1) of the Act includes a place of business in the Gaeseong Industrial District defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act on the Support of Gaeseong Industrial District. <Newly Inserted on May 10, 2016; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019>
  (5) "Income…prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-24 (2) of the Act means income calculated according to the following formula. In such cases, "turnover" in the formula means the turnover generated through the management of the same or similar line of business under each subparagraph of Article 104-24 (6) of the Act; and if the income calculated according to the calculation formula exceeds the income generated during the relevant taxable year at the new place of business after relocation (if an existing place of business was expanded, it means the income generated from the expanded part; hereafter in this paragraph, the same shall apply), it shall be deemed that there is no excess amount. <Newly Inserted on Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Where a place of business is relocated pursuant to paragraph (1) 1:
  Income generated during the relevant taxable year from the new place of business after relocation × Turnover from the overseas place of business during the taxable year in which the business relocated to the Republic of Korea commenced, as converted as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Economy and Finance in consideration of exchange rate, etc./Turnover generated during the relevant taxable year from the new place of business after relocation.
  2. Where a place of business is relocated pursuant to paragraph (1) 2:
  Income generated during the relevant taxable year from the place of business after relocation × Turnover from the overseas place of business during the taxable year in which the overseas business was transferred or closed, as converted as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Economy and Finance in consideration of exchange rate, etc./Turnover generated during the relevant taxable year from the new place of business after relocation
  (6) "Income…prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-24 (3) of the Act means income calculated according to the following formula. In such cases, "turnover" in the formula means the turnover generated through the management of the same or similar line of business under each subparagraph of Article 104-24 (6) of the Act; and if the income calculated according to the calculation formula exceeds the income generated during the relevant taxable year at the new place of business after relocation (if an existing place of business was expanded, it means an income generated from the expanded part; hereafter in this paragraph, the same shall apply), it shall be deemed that there is no excess amount. <Newly Inserted on Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Where a new business is established in the Republic of Korea pursuant to paragraph (3) 1:
  Income generated during the relevant taxable year from the new place of business after relocation × Turnover from the overseas place of business during the taxable year in which the business relocated to the Republic of Korea commenced, as converted as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Economy and Finance in consideration of exchange rate, etc./Turnover generated during the relevant taxable year from the new place of business after relocation.
  2. Where a place of business is established or expanded in the Republic of Korea pursuant to paragraph (3) 2:
  Income generated during the relevant taxable year from the place of business after repatriation × Downsized production capacity of the overseas place of business, as calculated by converting the amount equivalent to the production capacity confirmed by the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Economy and Finance in consideration of exchange rate, etc./Turnover generated during the relevant taxable year from the new place of business after repatriation
  (7) An amount of tax payable under 104-24 (4) of the Act shall be calculated as follows: <Amended on Feb. 17, 2021>
  1. In cases of Article 104-24 (4) 1 of the Act: A tax amount by with the tax was reduced or exempted within three years retroactively from the date of business closure (or the date of closure of the expanded part) or the date of dissolution of the corporation;
  2. In cases of Article 104-24 (4) 2 of the Act: The full amount of income tax or corporate tax reduced or exempted under Article 104-24 (2) of the Act;
  3. In cases of Article 104-24 (4) 3 of the Act: A tax amount by which the tax was reduced or exempted retroactively within three years from the date the business commenced at the established or expanded overseas place of business.
  (8)"Where the national fails to transfer or close the place of business operated in a foreign country, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-24 (4) 2 of the Act means a case that does not meet the requirements of paragraph (1). <Amended on Feb. 15, 2013; May. 10, 2016; Feb. 27 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021>
  (9)"Where a person who reduced a place of business operated in a foreign country extends the place of business again after receiving a tax reduction or exemption under paragraph (3), as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-24 (4) 3 of the Act means where an enterprise that meets the requirements of paragraph (3) 2 establishes a new overseas place of business or expand an existing overseas place of business during the period of tax reduction or exemption under Article 104-24 (3) of the Act. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 17, 2021>
  (10) In Article 104-24 (6) 2 of the Act, the term "where similarity of business types has been confirmed as prescribed by Presidential Decree" means the type of business operated at the place of business before the relocation or reinstatement and the place of business after the relocation or reinstatement on the basis of the major classification under the Korean Standard Industrial Classification are the same, in which case the similarity of business type between the places of business is confirmed by the Support Committee for Repatriating Enterprises under Article 6 of the Act on Assistance to Korean Off-Shore Enterprises in Repatriation. In such cases, necessary matters concerning the criteria, procedures, etc. for determining similarity shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 29, 2024>
  (11) The scope of the extension under Article 104-24 (7) of the Act shall be the cases falling under any of the following: <Newly Inserted on Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Where the total floor area of the relevant place of business increases as a result of installing new fixed assets for business use, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance;
  2. Where the quantity of fixed assets for business use increases as a result of installing new fixed assets for business use: Provided, That if the place of business is a factory prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, relevant cases shall be limited to those where new fixed assets for business use are installed in an area confirmed as an unused space according to public notice issued by the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy pursuant to Article 6 (2) 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Assistance to Korean Off-Shore Enterprises in Repatriation; but if the place of business is not a factory, such cases shall be limited to those where new production facilities necessary for business performance are installed.
  (12) Separate accounting under Article 104-24 (7) of the Act shall be carried out by applying Article 143 (1) of the Act mutatis mutandis and separating income generated from the expanded part from income generated from the pre-existing part before the expansion for the purposes of accounting. <Newly Inserted on Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 29, 2024>
  (13) A person who wishes to be granted a tax reduction or exemption under Article 104-24 (1) through (3) of the Act shall submit an application for the tax reduction or exemption, a statement of tax reduction or exemption, and other necessary documents, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with the tax return. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2013; May. 10, 2016; Feb. 7 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Apr. 14, 2020; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 29, 2024>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Dec. 30, 2010]

Article 104-22 (Tax Credits for Electronic Commerce of Petroleum Products) (1)"Electronic payment network prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause of Article 104-25 (1) of the Act means the electronic payment network for petroleum products operated by the Korea Exchange under Article 15 of the Addenda to the partial amendment (Act No. 11845) to the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act. <Amended on Aug. 27, 2013; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 11, 2020>
  (2)"Person designated by Presidential Decree, among petroleum distributors" in the main clause of Article 104-25 (1) of the Act means any of the following persons: <Amended on Feb. 11. 2020>
  1. A general distributor defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of thePetroleum and Alternative Fuel Business Act (excluding cases where petroleum products are supplied by a general distributor through the electronic payment network for petroleum products under paragraph (1));
  2. A gas station defined in subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of thePetroleum and Alternative Fuel Business Act;
  3. A general retail shop defined in subparagraph 4 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of thePetroleum and Alternative Fuel Business Act;
  (3) Any person who intends to be granted a tax credit of income tax or corporate tax under Article 104-25 of the Act shall file his/her tax return and an application for tax credit in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017>
  [This Article Newly Inserted by Act No. Feb. 2, 2012]

Article 104-23 (Inclusion of Claims in Deductible Expenses Following Revocation of Authorization for Establishment of Improvement Project Associations) "Where the constructor, etc. renounces all claims against the association, etc., as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-26 (1) 2 of the Act means where such constructor, etc. submits his/her tax return and a certification of renouncement of claims, in which the following matters are stated, to the head of a tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment. In such cases, the designer, constructor, or specialized manager of a rearrangement project shall be deemed to have declared his/her intention to exempt the association, etc. from claims, and the head of the competent tax office in receipt of the certificate shall immediately forward a copy of such certificate to the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu: <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 9, 2018>
  1. Amount of claims and the relevant evidentiary documents;
  2. Details of the renouncement of claims;
  3. Matters prescribed by municipal ordinance of a City/Do pursuant to subparagraph 3 of Article 133 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 21, 2014]

Article 104-24 Deleted. <Feb. 13, 2018>

Article 104-25 (Special Taxation for 2018 PyeongChang Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games) (1)"Foreign corporations prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-28 (1) 4 of the Act means the following: <Amended on Feb. 7, 2017; Jan. 9, 2018>
  1. The International Sports Federation or the International Sports Federation of the Disabled for each Olympic sport;
  2. The World Anti-Doping Agency;
  3. The Court of Arbitration for Sport;
  4. The Olympic cultural heritage foundation, the broadcast marketing company, and Olympic channel service company established by the International Olympic Committee;
  5. Organizations established by the International Paralympic Committee to promote and support sports activities of persons with disabilities;
  6. Business entities that use the emblem of the International Olympic Committee under a contract entered into with the International Olympic Committee to measure the time and scores of each competition or to operate the information system for the management of competitions (limited to where they have no place of business in the Republic of Korea);
  7. Rights Holding Broadcasters (RHBs) of the 2018 PyeongChang Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games by region.
  (2) A business operator who wishes to be granted a deduction of input tax amount pursuant to Article 104-28 (5) of the Act shall file a report (including filing it through the Home Tax Service Network) on the deduction of a deemed input tax amount in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance along with an aggregate invoice for each purchaser under Article 163 of the Income Tax Act or Article 121 of the Corporate Tax Act when filing a return under Article 48 or 49 of the Value-Added Tax Act. In such cases, if the following information is not entered in the report on the deduction of a deemed input tax amount or the details of the transaction is different from the fact, no input tax shall be deducted: <Newly Inserted on Jan. 9, 2018>
