Article 104-27 (Tax Credits on Shipping Companies and Shippers Certified as Excellent Shipping Companies) (1)"Company prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 104-30 (1) of the Act means a company that has a turnover in the immediately preceding taxable year. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (2) Freight charges and sea freight charges under Article 104_30 (1) of the Act shall be expenses paid to persons providing scheduled overseas cargo transportation services referred to in subparagraph 2 of Article 23 of the Marine Transportation Act, which meet all of the following requirements that:
  1. The expenses shall be those paid for the movement of goods exported or imported under subparagraph 3 or 4 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Foreign Trade Act;
  2. The expenses shall be those paid for transportation in the section stated in the bill of lading and other documents certifying the transportation contract concluded with a person providing scheduled overseas cargo transportation services.
  (3) A person who intends to apply for a tax credit pursuant to Article 104-30 (2) of the Act shall submit an application for the tax credit and a statement of the tax credit amount, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with the tax return.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 11, 2020]

Article 104-28 (Income Deductions for Project Financing Investment Companies) (1)"Distributable profit prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 104-31 (1) of the Act means an amount calculated in accordance with Article 86-3 (1) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act. <Amended on Feb. 15, 2022>
  (2) An investment company similar to any of those referred to in Article 51-2 (1) of the Income Tax Act shall be deemed to meet the requirements of Article 104-31 (1) 1 of the Act when it distributes to its stockholders its profits from a housing construction project jointly performed with a housing construction business entity in accordance with the Housing Act by using its assets for the housing construction project.
  (3)"Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-31 (1) 5 of the Act means the following requirements that:
  1. At least one incorporator shall meet any of the following criteria:
    (a) A financial company, etc. falling under any of subparagraphs 1 through 4, 6 through 13, and 24 of Article 61 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act;
    (b) the National Pension Service under the National Pension Act (limited cases of an investment company performing a public-private partnership project in a manner prescribed in subparagraph 2 of Article 4 of the Act on Public-Private Partnerships in Infrastructure);
  2. An incorporator falling under subparagraph 1 (a) or (b) shall make a contribution equivalent to at least 5/100 of the capital (if two or more incorporators fall under subparagraph 1 (a) or (b), their contributions shall be aggregated).
  (4)"Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-31 (1) 8 of the Act means the following requirements that:
  1. The capital shall be at least five billion won: Provided, That, in cases of an investment company performing a public-private partnership project in the manner prescribed in subparagraph 2 of Article 4 of the Act on Public-Private Partnerships in Infrastructure, the capital shall be at least one billion won;
  2. Services for the management, administration, and disposition of assets shall be entrusted to a person falling under any of the following (hereafter in this Article referred to as"asset management company"): Provided, That, in cases of the proviso of subparagraph 6, services for a trust contract under Article 4 (1) 1 of the Act on Sale of Building Units shall be entrusted to a company entrusted with fund management under subparagraph 3:
    (a) A corporation that has invested in the company;
    (b) A corporation established solely or jointly by a person who has invested in the company;
  3. Fund management shall be entrusted with a financial company, etc. engaged in a trust business under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as"company entrusted with fund management");
  4. Stockholders shall meet the following requirements. In such cases,"incorporator" shall be construed as"stockholder";
  5. A report on the establishment of a shell company with the following information stated thereon shall be submitted to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, within two months from the registration date of incorporation, along with documents attached thereto in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance:
    (a) Business objectives in the articles of incorporation;
    (b) Names and resident registration numbers of directors and auditors;
    (c) The name of the asset management company;
    (d) The name of the company entrusted with fund management;
  6. The asset management company and the company entrusted with fund management shall not be the same person: Provided, That, this shall not apply to cases where the relevant company has entered into a trust contract and agency contract with the company entrusted with fund management (the relevant company shall not be a controlling stockholder, etc. under Article 43 (7) of the Enforcement Decree of the Corporate Tax Act, and the investment ratio shall be less than 10/100) pursuant to Article 4 (1) 1 of the Act on the Sale of Building Units.
  (5) If any director, auditor, or stockholder of of a corporation falling under Article 104-31 (1) of the Act ceases to meet the requirements of Article 104-31 (1) 6 and 7 of the Act and paragraph (4) 4 of this Article after making a report pursuant to paragraph (4) 5 of this Article, but the corporation subsequently meets the requirements within one month from the date of occurrence of the cause of failure to meet the requirements, the corporation shall be deemed to continuously meet the requirements.
  (6) If a change occurs in any information referred to in paragraph (4) 5 after a corporation falling under Article 104-31 (1) of the Act makes a report pursuant to that subparagraph, the corporation shall report the change, within two weeks from the date of occurrence of such change, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment by submitting a report on the change in the shell company and documents attached thereto, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
  (7) Deleted. <Feb. 28, 2023>
  (8) A corporation that wishes to be granted an income deduction under Article 104-31 (1) of the Act shall submit an application for the income deduction in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with the tax return under Article 60 of the Corporate Tax Act.
  (9) A corporation falling under the proviso of Article 51-2 (2) 1 of the Corporate Tax Act shall, when applying for a tax deduction, attach a written confirmation of the application of special case of taxation on partnership enterprise and partnership taxation status in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance submitted by the deadline for reporting pursuant to Article 100-23 (1) of the Act from the partnership enterprise that received the dividends (including the higher-level partnerships if all or part of the partners constitute the higher-level partnerships under Article 100-15 (3) of the Act), in addition to the documents pursuant to paragraph (8). <Amended on Feb. 29, 2024>
