Article 104-29 (Tax Credits for Submission of Tax Data concerning Service Providers) (1)"Amount prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 104-32 (1) of the Act means the aggregate of the amounts calculated by multiplying the number of service providers listed in each tax data submitted pursuant to Article 173 (1) of the Income Tax Act (limited to the number of service providers whose personal information and the period of service provision are all stated pursuant to Article 224 (3) of the Enforcement Decree of the Income Tax Act) by 300 won. In such cases, an aggregate of less than 10,000 won shall be deemed 10,000 won, but if an aggregate exceeds two million won, the excess amount shall be deemed nil. <Amended on Feb. 28, 2023>
  (2) A person who wishes to be granted a tax credit pursuant to Article 104-32) (1) of the Act shall submit an application for the tax credit and a statement of the tax credit, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with the tax return.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Nov. 9, 2021]

Article 104-30 (Special Cases concerning Inclusion of Loans paid to Overseas Construction Subsidiaries in Deductible Expenses) (1) "Overseas construction subsidiary prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 104-33 (1) of the Act means corporations that meet all of the following requirements:
  1. It shall be a local corporation under subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Overseas Construction Promotion Act;
  2. It shall be a corporation in which an overseas construction business operator referred to in paragraph (2) 5 of the Overseas Construction Promotion Act invests not less than 90/100 of the total amount of investment or owns not less than 90/100 of the total number of issued stocks (if the overseas construction company is created through a split-off, it includes the cases where the split-off entity is a holding company and invests not less than 90/100 of the total amount of investment or holds not less than 90/100 of the total number of issued shares of the overseas construction company).
  (2) The term "claims prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the main clause, with the exception of subparagraphs, of Article 104-33 (1) of the Act, means claims accruing from labor costs paid by an overseas construction business operator to executive officers and employees dispatched to an overseas construction subsidiary on behalf the overseas construction subsidiary.
  (3) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree where it is deemed remarkably difficult to collect" in Article 104-33 (1) 4 of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where the overseas construction subsidiary has continuously eroded capital for 10 years immediately before the end of the business year in which the allowance for bad debt is included in deductible expenses;
  2. In cases similar to subparagraph 1, where it is confirmed by an overseas bond collection agency prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance that it is impossible to collect loans, etc. of overseas construction subsidiaries under the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 104-33 (1) of the Act.
  (4) A person who intends to be subject to Article 104-33 (1) of the Act shall, when filing a return under Article 60 of the Corporate Tax Act, attach documents verifying the fact that the case falls under any subparagraph of paragraph (3) to a written application for special cases of inclusion in deductible expenses prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and submit them to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 29, 2024]

