  Articles 116-19 (Special Cases concerning Indirect Taxes on Goods of Bonded Stores Installed on Passway Entering into Korea)  (1) Where an entrepreneur directly supplies goods manufactured and processed at his/her place of manufacture (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"domestic tax-free goods") to a bonded store referred to in the proviso of Article 196 (1) 1 and Article 196 (2) of the Customs Act (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"bonded store"), he/she shall be granted an exemption (in the case of value-added tax, referring to the application of zero tax rate; hereafter in this Article, the same shall apply) from the value-added tax and liquor tax on such goods under Article 121-14 (3) of the Act. <Amended on Feb. 17, 2021>
  (2) A person who wishes to be granted an exemption from value-added tax under paragraph (1) shall record the supply results of domestic tax-free goods in the relevant period of return, in a statement on the results of supply to bonded stores in the form prescribed by the Commissioner of the National Tax Service, and shall submit such statement to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of business after obtaining confirmation from the person who has received a license under the proviso of Article 176-2 (1) of the Customs Act (hereafter in this Article, referred to as"bonded store operator"), when he/she files a return on tax base and the amount of tax payable or the amount of tax refundable under Articles 48 and 49 of the Value-Added Tax Act.
  (3) A person who wishes to granted an exemption from liquor tax under paragraph (1) shall file an application for approval of tax exemption on the relevant liquor with the head of the competent tax office, applying mutatis mutandisArticle 20 (1) and (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Liquor Tax Act. <Amended on Feb. 17, 2021>
  (4) Upon carrying the liquor, value-added tax and liquor tax on which are exempted under paragraph (1), into a bonded store, the bonded store operator shall submit a report of carry-in of the liquor in the form prescribed by the Commissioner of the National Tax Service to the head of the competent tax office within five days from the carry-in date.
  (5) Where any goods exempted from value-added tax or liquor tax under Article 121-14 (1) and (2) of the Act falls under any of the following cases, the head of the competent tax office shall collect the exempted value-added tax or liquor tax from the person who has conducted the relevant act: <Amended on Feb. 17, 2021>
