CHAPTER V-3 SPECIAL TAXATION TO DEVELOP ENTERPRISE CITIES AND TO SUPPORT REGIONAL DEVELOPMENT PROJECT ZONES

Article 116-21 (Reduction or Exemption of Corporate Tax for Start-Up Enterprises in Enterprise City Development Zones) (1) An investment eligible for the reduction of, or exemption from, the corporate tax or income tax under Article 121-17 (1) 1, 3, 5, 8, or 9 of the Act means an investment for establishing a new facility in compliance with the standards for the investment amount and for the number of full-time employees in subparagraph 1 to operate a business referred to in any subparagraph of Article 116-2 (17) in the area referred to in any item of subparagraph 2: <Amended on Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. Standards for the investment amount and the standards for the number of full-time employees:
    (a) In cases of a business falling under Article 116-2 (17) 1, 4, or 5: The investment amount shall be at least two billion won, and the number of full-time employees shall be at least 30 persons;
    (b) In cases of a business falling under Article 116-2 (17) 2: The investment amount shall be at least 500 million won, and the number of full-time employees shall be at least ten persons;
    (c) In cases of a business falling under Article 116-2 (17) 3: The investment amount shall be at least one billion won, and the number of full-time employees shall be at least 15 persons;
  2. Investment area:
    (a) An enterprise city development zone defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities (hereafter in this Article referred to as"enterprise city development zone");
    (b) A regional development project zone designated under Article 11 of the Regional Development Assistance Act (limited to the regional development projects designated under Article 7 (1) 1 of that Act; hereafter in this Article referred to as"regional development project zone") or a regional promotion area designated under Article 67 of that Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as"regional promotion area");
    (c) The scope approved and publicly notified under Article 11 (5) and (8) of the Special Act on Support for Areas Adjacent to Districts Granted to the United States Armed Forces in Korea and Article 12 of the Enforcement Decree of that Act (hereafter in this Article referred to as"scope of projects for development of areas, etc. adjacent to a granted district"), among areas within undeveloped areas defined in subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Regional Development Assistance Act;
    (d) The special marine exposition district designated and publicly notified under Article 15 (1) of the Special Act on the Commemoration of and Follow-Up on the Expo 2012 Yeosu Korea (hereafter in this Article referred to as"special marine exposition district");
    (e) The Saemangeum investment promotion district designated pursuant to Article 11-5 of the Special Act on Promotion and Support for Saemangeum Project (hereafter in this Article referred to as"Saemangeum investment promotion district’).
    (f) Special economic zones for peace designated pursuant to Article 8 of the Act on the Designation and Operation of Special Economic Zones for Peace (hereinafter referred to as "Special Economic Zones for Peace").
  (2) An investment eligible for the reduction of, or exemption from, the corporate tax or income tax under Article 121-17 (1) 2, 4, 6, 7, or 10 of the Act means any investment made in a project for developing an enterprise city development zone in accordance with the relevant enterprise city development plan formulated under Article 11 of the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities or in any of the following projects, total development cost of which is at least 50 billion won: <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. A regional development project executed by a project implementer designated under Article 19 of the Regional Development Assistance Act to develop a regional development project zone or a regional promotion area;
  2. A project executed by a project implementer designated under Article 10 (1) of the Special Act on Support for Areas Adjacent to Districts Granted to the United States Armed Forces in Korea pursuant to paragraph (2) of that Article in an undeveloped area defined in subparagraph 5 of Article 2 of the Regional Development Assistance Act;
  3. A development project executed by a project implementer designated under Article 18 (1) of the Special Act on the Commemoration of and Follow-Up on the Expo 2012 Yeosu Korea to develop the special marine exposition district;
  4. The Saemangeum Project executed by a project implementer designated under Article 8 (1) of the Special Act on Promotion of the Saemangeum Project.
  5. A development project for a special economic zone for peace that is implemented by a development project implementer designated pursuant to Article 15 of the Act on the Designation and Operation of Special Peace Economic Zones.
  (3) Income eligible for tax reduction or exemption for the business activities conducted by an enterprise that starts its business or establishes a new place of business in an enterprise city development zone, a regional development project zone, a regional promotion area, the scope of project for development of areas, etc. adjacent to a granted district, a special marine exposition district, the Saemangeum investment promotion district, or special economic zone for peace referred to in Article 121-17 (1) 1, 3, 5, 8, or 9 of the Act means the income directly accruing from the facilities in which the enterprise has made investments in the relevant area, in order to conduct the business eligible for tax reduction or exemption under paragraph (1). <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  (4)"Cumulative investments prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 121-17 (4) 1 of the Act means the aggregate of investments in the business assets prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance by the relevant taxable years in which a reduction or exemption of corporate tax or income tax is granted under Article 121-17 (2) of the Act. <Newly Inserted on Dec. 30, 2010>
  (5) The amount of the income tax or corporate tax to be paid under Article 121-17 (6) of the Act shall be calculated by the following formula (where the amount is a negative, it shall be deemed nil; if the number of full-time employees has decreased for the two consecutive years after the taxable year in which the tax reduction or exemption is granted ends, such amount to be paid in the second taxable year means an amount less the amount paid in the first taxable year); and such amount shall be paid as income tax or corporate tax, when filing the tax return of the taxable year in which the number of full-time employees has decreased: <Newly Inserted on Dec. 30, 2010; Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 28, 2023>
  The aggregate of amounts of tax reduced or exempted under Article 121-17 (4) 2 of the Act within two taxable years immediately preceding the taxable year in which the number of full-time employees of the relevant enterprise has decreased - [the number of full-time employees of the place of business eligible for tax reduction or exemption in the taxable year in which the number of full-time employees has decreased × 15 million won (or 20 million won in cases of a full-time youth employee or a service business referred to in Article 121-17 (4) 2 of the Act is applicable)]
  (6) For the purposes of Article 121-17 (4) and (6) of the Act, Article 11-2 (6) and (7) shall apply mutatis mutandis to the scope of full-time employees and of full-time youth employees and the method for calculating the number of full-time employees and the number of full-time youth employees. <Amended on Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 28, 2023>
  (7) A person who wishes to be granted a reduction or exemption of corporate tax or income tax under Article 121-17 (2) of the Act shall file an application for tax reduction or exemption, in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the head of the competent tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, along with his/her tax return. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Dec. 30, 2010>
  (8)"Service business prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 121-17 (4) 2 of the Act means the service business referred to in Article 23 (4). <Newly Inserted on Feb. 7, 2017; Feb. 12, 2019>
  (9)"Zone prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 121-17 (1) 3 of the Act means the scope of project for development of areas, etc. adjacent to a granted district. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 12, 2019>
  (10) The tax reduction or exemption under paragraph (1) shall not apply to taxable years in which an enterprise eligible under that paragraph fails to meet the criteria for the number of persons to be employed under the same subparagraph. <Newly Inserted on Feb. 12, 2019>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 19, 2005]
  [Title Amended on Feb. 18, 2010]

Article 116-22 (Post Management of Special Taxation for Golf Courses in Enterprise Cities) The Metropolitan City Mayor or the head of the Si or Gun (excluding the head of a Gun under the jurisdiction of a Metropolitan City) having jurisdiction over a tourism-centered enterprise city (including tourism-leisure-type enterprise cites designated under subparagraph 1 (c) of Article 2 of the former Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities as at the time the Special Act on the Development of Enterprise Cities (Act No. 13372) enters into force; the same shall apply hereafter in this Article) shall take the following measures pursuant to Article 121-18 (2) of the Act: <Amended on Dec. 22, 2015>
  1. To establish and operate the deliberative committee on admission fees for golf courses in order to deliberate on whether to reflect the tax cuts under Article 121-18 (1) of the Act in admission fees for golf courses located in tourism-centered enterprise cities;
  2. To take corrective measures, such as reducing the admission fees, if he/she deems that the deliberative committee on the admission fees for golf courses fails to properly reflect the tax cuts in admission fees.
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 19, 2005]

Article 116-23 (Additional Collection of Reduced or Exempted Tax Amount) The additional collection of the corporate tax or income tax under Article 121-19 (1) of the Act shall be made according to the following standards: <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  1. In cases falling under Article 121-19 (1) 1, 2 and 4 through 12 of the Act: Additionally collect the amount tax that has been reduced or exempted within five years from the date of cancellation of designation, date of revocation of approval of implementation, date of business closure, or date of discontinuance;
  2. In cases falling under Article 121-19 (1) 3 of the Act: Additionally collect the total amount of tax that has been reduced or exempted. In such cases, the criteria for the number of persons to be employed under subparagraphs of Article 116-21 (1) shall be met in at least one taxable year out of the period until the end of the taxable years not exceeding two years after the end of the taxable year in which the first income accrues from the relevant project eligible for reduction or exemption (if no income accrues from the relevant project until the taxable year in which the third anniversary of the project commencement date falls, referring to the taxable year in which the third anniversary falls).
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 19, 2005]

Article 116-24 (Notification, etc. of Causes for Additional Collection of Taxes) (1) When the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, and the head of a local government becomes aware of the fact that any of the causes for additionally collecting taxes under Article 121-19 (1) of the Act has occurred, he/she shall, without delay, notify the head of the competent tax office thereof. <Amended on Feb. 29, 2008; Mar. 23, 2013>
  (2) The date of permanent closure of business reported under Article 8 (6) of the Value-Added Tax Act shall be deemed the date of permanent closure of the business or place of business of an enterprise that started up a business or established a place of business in an enterprise city development zone, a regional development project zone, a regional promotion area, the special marine exhibition district, or the scope of projects for development of areas adjacent to a granted district, Saemangeum Investment Promotion Zone, and peace economic zone, etc. defined under Article 121-19 (1) 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, or 12 of the Act (hereafter referred to as "start-up business, etc." in this Article). <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Jun. 28, 2013; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 17, 2021; Feb. 29, 2024>
  (3) Income eligible for tax reduction or exemption for the business activities engaged in by an enterprise that starts its business or establishes a new place of business in an enterprise city development zone, a regional development project zone, a regional promotion area, a special marine exposition district, the scope of project for development of areas, etc. adjacent to a granted district, the Saemangeum investment promotion district, or special peace economic zone referred to in Article 121-17 (1) 1, 3, 5, 8, or 9 of the Act means the income directly accruing from the facilities in which the enterprise has made investments in the relevant area, in order to engage in the business eligible for tax reduction or exemption under paragraph (1). <Amended on Feb. 18, 2010; Feb. 15, 2013; Feb. 3, 2015; Feb. 5, 2016; Feb. 12, 2019; Feb. 28, 2023; Feb. 29, 2024>
  [This Article Newly Inserted on Feb. 19, 2005]

