Article 116-37 (Special Taxation on Enterprises Relocating to Special Opportunity Development Zone) (1) "Business real estate prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 121-34 (1) of the Act means real estate used for the following purposes:
  1. The head office of the company concerned;
  2. Factory under Article 54 (1);
  3. A company-affiliated research institute pursuant to Article 14-2 (1) of the Basic Research Promotion and Technology Development Support Act;
  4. Sites and buildings of the data centers under Article 40 of the Framework Act on Intelligent Informatization.
  (2) "Amount calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the provisions, with the exception of the the subparagraphs, Article 121-34 (1) of the Act means the amount calculated by multiplying the amount specified in subparagraph 1 by the rate specified in subparagraph 2 (hereafter referred to as "amount equivalent to capital gains" in this Article).
  1. Any of the following amounts:
    (a) Corporation: The amount obtained by deducting the total amount of losses carried forward under Article 13 (1) 1 of the Corporate Tax Act as of the end date of the business year immediately preceding the business year in which the date of transfer of the former business real estate is transferred, from the gains on the transfer of business real estate under the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 121-34 (1) of the Act (hereafter referred to as "former business real estate" in this Article);
    (b) Residents: Gains on the transfer of former business real estate;
  2. The ratio of the acquisition value of the business real estate located in the special opportunity development zone (hereinafter referred to as "real estate for new business") out of the transfer value of the former business real estate for business (up to 100/100).
  (3) In applying paragraph (2), if the new business real estate is not acquired by the end date of the taxable year in which the transfer date of the previous business real estate falls, the acquisition value of the new business real estate shall be the estimated value on the (planned) transfer statement under paragraph (8) (hereinafter referred to as "estimated acquisition value" in this Article).
  (4) Where a corporation is subject to Article 121-34 (1) of the Act, the amount equivalent to the gains on transfer out of the acquisition value of the real estate for new business shall be included in the loss expenses as a temporary depreciation allowance or advanced depreciation provision according to the following classification:
  1. Depreciable assets: Lump sum of temporary depreciation allowance;
  2. Assets other than those referred to in subparagraph 1: Advanced depreciation provision;
  (5) "Amount calculated as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 121-34 (3) of the Act means an amount classified in following subparagraphs:
  1. A corporation: The amount specified in any of the following items:
    (a) Where a temporary depreciation allowance is recorded under paragraph (4) 1, the balance remaining after offsetting the depreciation expenses;
    (b) Where it is appropriated as an advanced depreciation provision under paragraph (4) 2, the entire amount of the advanced depreciation provision;
  2. A resident: The entire amount of unpaid capital gains tax;
  (6) "Where it is deemed that a project has not been transferred, as prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 121-34 (3) 3 of the Act means the case where the value of the real estate for the new business that is disposed of, or not used for the relevant business, by a Korean national subject to the same paragraph (1) of that Article is not less than a half of the total value of the new business real estate.
  (7) In applying Article 121-34 (1) of the Act, if the amount equivalent to capital gains calculated based on the estimated acquisition value is not included in the gross income or the taxation is deferred, an amount applied in excess of the amount calculated pursuant to paragraph (2) based on the actual acquisition value shall be included in the gross income of the taxable year in which the date of commencement of business by acquiring real estate for new business or shall be paid as capital gains tax. In such cases, the latter part of Article 33 (3) of the Act shall apply mutatis mutandis to the amount to be included in gross income or to be paid as capital gains tax.
  (8) A corporation that intends to be eligible under Article 121-34 (1) 1 of the Act shall submit a detailed statement of proceeds from transfer, detailed statement of adjustment of divided inclusion in the gross income, and detailed statement of (scheduled) relocation, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, at the time of filing a tax base return for the business year in which the transfer date of the former business real estate falls.
  (9) A resident who intends to be eligible for the deferment of taxation under Article 121-34 (1) 2 of the Act shall submit a written application for tax deferral and a detailed statement of (scheduled) relocation, in the forms prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment, at the time of filing a tax base return (including a provisional return) for the taxable year in which the transfer date of the former business real estate falls.
  (10) Where a person commences business by acquiring the real estate for new business after the application of paragraph (3), he/she shall submit a report on the completion of transfer prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to the head of the tax office having jurisdiction over the place of tax payment when he files a tax base return for the taxable year to which the commencement date of such business belongs.
