  (11) "Investor's death, or emigration to a foreign country, or unavoidable circumstances prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 121-35 (4) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where the account holder is dead or emigrates to a foreign country;
  2. Where the event referred to in any subparagraph of Article 81 (6) occurs to the account holder within six months prior to the date of termination;
  3. Where the collective investment scheme of a special opportunity development zone is dissolved.
  (12) A resident who intends to terminate the contract for any of the reasons specified in paragraph (11) shall submit a report on the special reason for termination, in the form prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, to the financial companies, etc. that manage the dedicated accounts under Article 121-35 (4) of the Act.
